{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CghrdfQmDL9W35Z4VNCKw","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01CyufMzj4H5Etn3bVeiCBpJ","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build__20261104-050244__x8ffc89/work/Gauntletdown-Gauntlet-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261104-050244/hub/README.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":892,"cache_read_input_tokens":150522,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":892},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9fe4bfc6-ee9b-4f5a-880a-60c3aeac1094","uuid":"e0361e46-7522-4ab3-bb42-5cf1c87bb890","timestamp":"2026-11-04T12:04:34.759Z","request_id":"req_011Cghrdf9tYBByQHgC9HQY6","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01CyufMzj4H5Etn3bVeiCBpJ":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build__20261104-050244__x8ffc89/work/Gauntletdown-Gauntlet-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261104-050244/hub/README.md"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CyufMzj4H5Etn3bVeiCBpJ","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# AI Hub Session Protocol v1\n2\t\n3\tAn **AI Hub session** is up to four players, each on their own device,\n4\tplaying rounds of games one after another. The hub runs everything around a\n5\tround: the invite, the lobby, the seats and names, the network, the clock, the\n6\tscoreboard and the results. This page defines how a game takes part in a\n7\tround, and how the copies of a game send data to each other.\n8\t\n9\t**https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/README.md**\n10\t\n11\tThe hub tests every game when it joins the library, with the same test\n12\tdescribed in *Test it*, and keeps a game that fails it out of sessions.\n13\t\n14\t- Client: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/session.js\n15\t- Harness: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/harness.html\n16\t\n17\tTo ask an agent for it, add this to the game's prompt:\n18\t\n19\t> This game must support AI Hub sessions. Follow\n20\t> https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/README.md\n21\t> (AI Hub Session Protocol v1) and pass the harness's automatic check.\n22\t\n23\t---\n24\t\n25\t## Modes\n26\t\n27\tA game declares one mode.\n28\t\n29\t| Mode | What each copy runs | What the copies send each other |\n30\t|---|---|---|\n31\t| `parallel` | its own copy of the round | nothing |\n32\t| `ghost` | its own copy of the round | each copy's own player: where it is and what it is doing |\n33\t| `shared-world` | one world for all players, run by the host's copy | what each player does, to the host; the world, from the host |\n34\t\n35\t- **Parallel**: every player plays their own copy of the round, from the same\n36\t  start. Each copy reports its score to the hub.\n37\t- **Ghost**: as parallel, and each copy also shows the other players'\n38\t  characters where they are, when they are in the same area of the game.\n39\t  Those characters do not affect anything in the copy that shows them.\n40\t- **Shared world**: all players play in one world. The host's copy runs that\n41\t  world; the other copies send it what their own player does, and show the\n42\t  world the host sends them.\n43\t\n44\tGames tagged with the older modes keep working: `race` is played as ghost,\n45\t`co-op` and `versus` as shared world.\n46\t\n47\t---\n48\t\n49\t## A round\n50\t\n51\t1. The hub loads the game on every player's device, and the players get 10\n52\t   to 30 seconds with the game's card: what the game is, how to win, the\n53\t   controls. The card is the hub's, from the game's tags, or the game's own\n54\t   (*The card*).\n55\t2. The game connects and calls `ready()`.\n56\t3. The round starts on the hub's clock, on every device at once.\n57\t4. The game reports how it goes.\n58\t5. The round ends when every player has a result, when the host of a shared\n59\t   world finishes it, or when the hub calls time. The hub shows the results\n60\t   over the game, then removes it.\n61\t\n62\t### Tags\n63\t\n64\tIn the game's `<head>`:\n65\t\n66\t```html\n67\t<meta name=\"hub:session\" content=\"1\">\n68\t<meta name=\"hub:session-players\" content=\"MIN-MAX\">\n69\t<meta name=\"hub:session-mode\" content=\"MODE\">\n70\t<meta name=\"hub:session-goal\" content=\"GOAL\">\n71\t<meta name=\"hub:session-howto\" content=\"CONTROLS\">\n72\t```\n73\t\n74\t- `hub:session-players`: the smallest and largest number of players the game\n75\t  takes in a session. The hub deals the game only when the number of players\n76\t  is in that range.\n77\t- `hub:session-mode`: `parallel`, `ghost` or `shared-world`.\n78\t- `hub:session-goal` and `hub:session-howto`: how to win and the game's\n79\t  controls, shown on the hub's card.\n80\t\n81\tOptional:\n82\t\n83\t- `hub:session-minutes`: how many minutes a round of the game takes. The hub\n84\t  shows it and uses it to decide when to call time.\n85\t- `hub:webgpu` with `required`: the game cannot run without WebGPU. The hub\n86\t  then deals it only when every player's browser has WebGPU.\n87\t\n88\t### The client\n89\t\n90\t[session.js](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/session.js)\n91\tis pasted into the game unmodified, as the first script in `<head>`, right\n92\tafter `<meta charset>`. In a session it:\n93\t\n94\t- seeds `Math.random`, in parallel and ghost, before any of the game's own\n95\t  scripts run, so it gives the same numbers on every copy;\n96\t- gives the game an empty `localStorage` and `sessionStorage` of its own, so\n97\t  nothing stored on the device carries into the round, and nothing the round\n98\t  stores reaches the device's own storage;\n99\t- hands `requestFullscreen()` and `exitFullscreen()` to the hub, which takes\n100\t  its whole page fullscreen; `document.fullscreenElement` and\n101\t  `fullscreenchange` follow the hub's page.\n102\t\n103\tThe hub replaces an unmodified copy of the client with each new version. An\n104\tedited copy is not replaced.\n105\t\n106\t### Joining\n107\t\n108\t- `AIHub.active` is `true` from the first line when the hub opened the page.\n109\t- In a session, the game opens straight into the round: no title screen,\n110\t  menus or prompts before it, other than its own card (*The card*).\n111\t- `AIHub.connect({ mode, seats: [min, max] })` returns a promise of the\n112\t  round's `info`, or of `null` when there is no hub after all; with `null`\n113\t  the game runs as it does on its own.\n114\t- `AIHub.ready()` is called once, when the game has loaded and the round can\n115\t  start, with no key press: the players answer the card.\n116\t- The round starts when the card's countdown ends or every player pressed\n117\t  Ready, and every game has called `ready()`. A game still loading then gets\n118\t  20 more seconds; after that its player sits the round out.\n119\t\n120\t`info` (also on `AIHub` after `connect()`):\n121\t\n122\t| Field | |\n123\t|---|---|\n124\t| `me` | this copy's player id |\n125\t| `players` | `[{ id, name, color }]`, ids `0..N-1` in seat order |\n126\t| `host`, `isHost` | the id of the copy that runs a shared world, and whether it is this one |\n127\t| `server` | `true` only on a copy that hosts a shared world with no player of its own |\n128\t| `mode`, `round`, `limitMs` | the mode, the round number, and the round's hard limit after the start |\n129\t| `seed` | a number, the same on every copy, behind `AIHub.rng(label)` |\n130\t\n131\tNames come from the hub and are never inserted into the page as HTML. Colours\n132\tfollow the seat: `#e8443a`, `#3b82f6`, `#22c55e`, `#f5b700`.\n133\t\n134\t### The card\n135\t\n136\tBefore every round the players get 10 to 30 seconds to learn what comes\n137\tnext and say when they are ready. By default the hub shows its own card over\n138\tthe game. A game can make the card its own, as part of the game:\n139\t\n140\t```js\n141\tAIHub.connect({ mode, seats, card: true });\n142\t```\n143\t\n144\tThe hub's card then steps aside when the game calls `ready()`, and the game's\n145\tscreen is the card until `start`. How it looks and sounds is the game's: its\n146\ttitle, its music, its world, the players lining up. Introduce the game the way\n147\tit deserves.\n148\t\n149\tWhile it is on, the card shows:\n150\t\n151\t- the game's name;\n152\t- the players, each in their colour, and which of them are ready;\n153\t- how to win the round;\n154\t- the controls this player will use;\n155\t- the time left, from the `card` event.\n156\t\n157\tAnd it takes two answers, from the keyboard, a controller, or a tap or click\n158\ton the card:\n159\t\n160\t- **Ready**: Enter, Cross (button 0), or a tap on Ready:\n161\t  `AIHub.answer('ready')`.\n162\t- **More time**: Triangle (button 3), a key the card names, or a tap on More\n163\t  time: `AIHub.answer('more')`. Answering `more` again takes it back.\n164\t\n165\tNothing done on the card changes the round. It has no menus, settings or\n166\tchoices, and play begins only at `start`. In parallel and ghost it draws no\n167\tnumbers from `Math.random`, which would change the round's start: use\n168\t`AIHub.rng('card')`.\n169\t\n170\t`card` arrives whenever it changes, and every second while the countdown runs:\n171\t\n172\t| Field | |\n173\t|---|---|\n174\t| `left` | milliseconds until the round starts by itself; `null` while paused or starting |\n175\t| `paused` | `true` while most players asked for more time |\n176\t| `starting` | `true` once the countdown is over or everyone is ready: `start` follows when every game has loaded |\n177\t| `ready` | the ids of the players who are ready |\n178\t| `asking` | how many players asked for more time (never who) |\n179\t| `asked` | `true` when this player asked for more time |\n180\t\n181\t### The start\n182\t\n183\t`start` arrives when the round starts. Play begins three seconds later, when\n184\t`AIHub.time()` reaches 0. `AIHub.time()` is the same timeline on every device,\n185\tgive or take about 15 ms: negative during the countdown, `-Infinity` before\n186\t`start`.\n187\t\n188\t### Reporting\n189\t\n190\t- `AIHub.progress({ score, label })`, in parallel and ghost: the player's\n191\t  standing during the round. `score` is a number, higher is ahead; `label` is\n192\t  text for the hub's scoreboard. The hub takes the latest about once a second.\n193\t- `AIHub.result({ time })` or `AIHub.result({ score })`, in parallel and\n194\t  ghost, once, when the player's round is over. `time` is milliseconds of\n195\t  `AIHub.time()`, lower wins; `score` is a number, higher wins.\n196\t- `AIHub.finish({ standings, scores, won })`, in a shared world, called once,\n197\t  by the host only:\n198\t  - `standings`: arrays of player ids, best first; players in the same array\n199\t    tie. It lists every player still in the round once; anyone left out is\n200\t    placed last.\n201\t  - `scores` (optional): `{ id: number }`, shown on the scoreboard.\n202\t  - `won` (optional): `true` or `false` when the round is a team result.\n203\t\n204\t### Time-up and the end\n205\t\n206\t- The hub may call time while the round is still going. On `time-up`, the\n207\t  game reports within `graceMs`: a `result()` in parallel and ghost, a\n208\t  `finish()` from the host in a shared world. A shared world with no\n209\t  `finish()` by then is void.\n210\t- `end` is the last message of a round. After it, the game takes no input and\n211\t  sends nothing, and its sound stops. The hub shows its results over the\n212\t  game, then removes it.\n213\t\n214\t| `end` reason | |\n215\t|---|---|\n216\t| `finished` | the round counted; `standings` is the final order |\n217\t| `void` | it didn't count (no result, a fatal error, skipped) |\n218\t| `host-left` | the host of a shared world left |\n219\t| `sat-out` | this player missed the ready deadline |\n220\t| `session-ended` | the session closed |\n221\t\n222\t### Leaving\n223\t\n224\t- `leave` arrives with `{ id, reason }` when a player leaves: `left`,\n225\t  `disconnected`, `not-ready` or `kicked`. It is final for the round.\n226\t- A parallel or ghost round goes on whoever leaves, the host included.\n227\t- A shared-world round is void when its host leaves, isn't ready, or has its\n228\t  tab hidden for more than 20 seconds.\n229\t- `AIHub.fail(message)`: the game cannot run in this browser. From the host\n230\t  of a shared world it voids the round; from any other copy it counts as\n231\t  that player leaving.\n232\t\n233\t### Scoring\n234\t\n235\t- Parallel and ghost: players with a `time` rank first, lowest first; then\n236\t  the rest by `score`. A player with no result is ranked by their last\n237\t  progress.\n238\t- Shared world: the host's `standings`. With `won`, the results show a team\n239\t  result instead of medals.\n240\t- Each player gets one point for every player they beat.\n241\t\n242\t`result()` and `finish()` may also carry `stats` and `awards`, shown with the\n243\tresults:\n244\t\n245\t- in `result()`: `stats` is `{ name: value }` and `awards` is\n246\t  `[{ title, detail }]`, for this player;\n247\t- in `finish()`: `stats` is `{ id: { name: value } }` and `awards` is\n248\t  `[{ id, title, detail }]`, for each player.\n249\t\n250\tPlaces and points come only from the standings, `time` and `score`.\n251\t\n252\t---\n253\t\n254\t## Sending data between copies\n255\t\n256\t### Parallel\n257\t\n258\tThe copies send nothing to each other. `send()` is not used.\n259\t\n260\t### Ghost\n261\t\n262\tEach copy sends its own player's position and what the player is doing to\n263\tthe other copies with `send()`. Each copy shows the other players' characters\n264\tonly while they are in the same area of the game as its own player, and those\n265\tcharacters do not affect its world. `Math.random` is seeded as in parallel.\n266\t\n267\t### Shared world\n268\t\n269\t- The host's copy (`AIHub.isHost`) runs the world. The other copies send the\n270\t  host what their own player does, and show the world the host sends them.\n271\t- The hub can run the host's copy with no player of its own: `AIHub.server`\n272\t  is `true` and `AIHub.me` is not among `AIHub.players`. The host's copy runs\n273\t  the world in that case too, with no local player, camera or input.\n274\t- `Math.random` is not seeded. `AIHub.rng(label)` gives the same numbers on\n275\t  every copy.\n276\t\n277\t### `send()` and `message`\n278\t\n279\t- `AIHub.send(data, { to, reliable })` sends `data` to every other copy, or\n280\t  to the one player `to`. It returns `false` when the message is dropped.\n281\t- `AIHub.on('message', (data, from) => …)` receives it; `from` is the\n282\t  sender's player id. A copy never receives its own messages. Messages sent\n283\t  before another copy has loaded are queued for it.\n284\t- `data` is JSON, at most 16 KB.\n285\t- At most 20 messages a second leave each copy, with bursts up to 40; the\n286\t  client drops the rest.\n287\t- Reliable messages (the default) arrive in the order they were sent.\n288\t  Messages sent with `reliable: false` may be lost or arrive out of order. An\n289\t  unreliable message larger than about 1,200 bytes travels as several packets\n290\t  and is lost whole if any of them is.\n291\t\n292\t---\n293\t\n294\t## Rules\n295\t\n296\tIn a session:\n297\t\n298\t- **Network only through the hub.** No WebSocket, WebRTC, or `fetch` to a\n299\t  game server or public broker. Loading the game's own files is fine.\n300\t- **No communication between players.** No chat, voice, emotes or custom\n301\t  names. Names come from the hub.\n302\t- **The page stays.** No `alert`, `confirm` or `prompt`; no `window.open`,\n303\t  new tabs or navigating away. Quitting, restarting or returning to a title\n304\t  screen does nothing; the hub starts and ends rounds.\n305\t- **Create + Options is the hub's.** On a controller, holding the two\n306\t  together opens the hub's corner bar; the game ignores Options while Create\n307\t  is held.\n308\t\n309\tEverything on this page applies only in a session (`AIHub.active`). Outside\n310\tone, the game is not affected.\n311\t\n312\t---\n313\t\n314\t## Test it\n315\t\n316\tThe harness plays the hub: it loads the game 1–4 times on a simulated network\n317\tand runs the checks the hub runs when a game joins the library. Serve it next\n318\tto the game:\n319\t\n320\t```bash\n321\tcurl -fsSO https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/harness.html\n322\tcurl -fsSO https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/bridge.js\n323\tcurl -fsSO https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/round.js\n324\tpython3 -m http.server 8000\n325\t```\n326\t\n327\tThen open `http://localhost:8000/harness.html?game=GAME.html&players=2&auto=1`.\n328\tThe hub's own test also runs ghost and shared-world games with\n329\t`&players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1`, again with\n330\t`&scenario=host-leave`, and shared worlds once more with\n331\t`&players=2&scenario=server`.\n332\t\n333\tThe checklist fills in as it runs. **A game passes when\n334\t`window.__hubCheck.pass` is true**; `document.body.dataset.complete` becomes\n335\t`\"true\"` at the end. It checks:\n336\t\n337\t- the tags, `connect()`, `ready()` with no key press, and the start;\n338\t- with the game's own card, that Enter answers Ready;\n339\t- parallel and ghost: `Math.random` the same on every copy, and progress from\n340\t  every copy; parallel sends nothing, ghost sends;\n341\t- shared world: traffic both ways, and a round hosted by a copy with no\n342\t  player of its own;\n343\t- a player leaving, the host leaving, time-up, a valid result, and every copy\n344\t  told the round ended;\n345\t- no protocol problems, errors, dialogs, popups or sockets.\n346\t\n347\t**New round**, **Time up**, **Remove player** and **Hide host tab** run the\n348\tcases by hand; clicking a player's frame gives it the keyboard and mouse.\n349\t`&limit=` sets the round's length in seconds and `&seed=` fixes the seed. The\n350\tgame is served from the harness's own origin.\n351\t\n352\tIn the AI Hub repository, `node scripts/hub-check.mjs <game>` runs the same\n353\tchecks with Playwright, then opens the game outside a session to see it still\n354\truns there.\n355\t\n356\t---\n357\t\n358\t## Reference\n359\t\n360\t### Tags\n361\t\n362\t| Tag | |\n363\t|---|---|\n364\t| `hub:session` | `1`: this protocol |\n365\t| `hub:session-players` | `MIN-MAX`: the number of players the game takes in a session |\n366\t| `hub:session-mode` | `parallel`, `ghost` or `shared-world` |\n367\t| `hub:session-goal` | how to win, shown on the hub's card |\n368\t| `hub:session-howto` | the controls, shown on the hub's card |\n369\t| `hub:session-minutes` | optional: how many minutes a round takes |\n370\t| `hub:webgpu` | optional: `required` when the game cannot run without WebGPU |\n371\t\n372\t### API\n373\t\n374\t| | |\n375\t|---|---|\n376\t| `AIHub.active` | `true` in a session, from the first line |\n377\t| `AIHub.connect({ mode, seats, card? })` | → `Promise<info \\| null>`; `null`: no hub. `card: true`: the game shows its own card |\n378\t| `AIHub.ready()` | once, when the round can start |\n379\t| `AIHub.answer('ready' \\| 'more')` | on the game's own card, before `start` |\n380\t| `AIHub.time()` | milliseconds since play began: negative in the countdown, `-Infinity` before `start` |\n381\t| `AIHub.on(event, fn)` | returns a function that removes the handler |\n382\t| `AIHub.progress({ score, label })` | parallel and ghost |\n383\t| `AIHub.result({ time \\| score, stats?, awards? })` | parallel and ghost, once |\n384\t| `AIHub.finish({ standings, scores?, won?, stats?, awards? })` | shared world, the host, once |\n385\t| `AIHub.send(data, { to, reliable })` | ghost and shared world |\n386\t| `AIHub.rng(label)` | a generator of numbers in `[0, 1)`, the same on every copy, one stream per label |\n387\t| `AIHub.seeded` | `true` when the client seeded `Math.random` |\n388\t| `AIHub.fail(message)` | the game cannot run in this browser |\n389\t\n390\t`AIHub.probe()` and `AIHub.inspect()` exist for older games; the hub does not\n391\tread them.\n392\t\n393\t| Event | Arguments |\n394\t|---|---|\n395\t| `card` | `{ left, paused, starting, ready, asking, asked }`, with the game's own card |\n396\t| `start` | `{ in }`: milliseconds until play begins |\n397\t| `message` | `data, from` |\n398\t| `leave` | `{ id, reason }` |\n399\t| `time-up` | `{ graceMs }` |\n400\t| `end` | `{ reason, standings }` |\n401\t\n402\tEvents that arrive before a handler is attached are kept, and delivered in\n403\torder when the first handler is attached. Fields and events a newer hub adds\n404\treach the game through the client unchanged.\n405\t\n406\t### Versions\n407\t\n408\tThis is protocol **1**, client **1.4.0**. Changes within version 1 only add:\n409\tgames on older clients keep working. A change that would break a game becomes\n410\tprotocol 2, with its own `hub:session` value.\n411\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9fe4bfc6-ee9b-4f5a-880a-60c3aeac1094","uuid":"11fe2dd1-a90a-4d6a-83ac-9750877654c7","timestamp":"2026-11-04T12:04:34.764Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build__20261104-050244__x8ffc89/work/Gauntletdown-Gauntlet-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261104-050244/hub/README.md","content":"# AI Hub Session Protocol v1\n\nAn **AI Hub session** is up to four players, each on their own device,\nplaying rounds of games one after another. The hub runs everything around a\nround: the invite, the lobby, the seats and names, the network, the clock, the\nscoreboard and the results. This page defines how a game takes part in a\nround, and how the copies of a game send data to each other.\n\n**https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/README.md**\n\nThe hub tests every game when it joins the library, with the same test\ndescribed in *Test it*, and keeps a game that fails it out of sessions.\n\n- Client: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/session.js\n- Harness: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/harness.html\n\nTo ask an agent for it, add this to the game's prompt:\n\n> This game must support AI Hub sessions. Follow\n> https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/README.md\n> (AI Hub Session Protocol v1) and pass the harness's automatic check.\n\n---\n\n## Modes\n\nA game declares one mode.\n\n| Mode | What each copy runs | What the copies send each other |\n|---|---|---|\n| `parallel` | its own copy of the round | nothing |\n| `ghost` | its own copy of the round | each copy's own player: where it is and what it is doing |\n| `shared-world` | one world for all players, run by the host's copy | what each player does, to the host; the world, from the host |\n\n- **Parallel**: every player plays their own copy of the round, from the same\n  start. Each copy reports its score to the hub.\n- **Ghost**: as parallel, and each copy also shows the other players'\n  characters where they are, when they are in the same area of the game.\n  Those characters do not affect anything in the copy that shows them.\n- **Shared world**: all players play in one world. The host's copy runs that\n  world; the other copies send it what their own player does, and show the\n  world the host sends them.\n\nGames tagged with the older modes keep working: `race` is played as ghost,\n`co-op` and `versus` as shared world.\n\n---\n\n## A round\n\n1. The hub loads the game on every player's device, and the players get 10\n   to 30 seconds with the game's card: what the game is, how to win, the\n   controls. The card is the hub's, from the game's tags, or the game's own\n   (*The card*).\n2. The game connects and calls `ready()`.\n3. The round starts on the hub's clock, on every device at once.\n4. The game reports how it goes.\n5. The round ends when every player has a result, when the host of a shared\n   world finishes it, or when the hub calls time. The hub shows the results\n   over the game, then removes it.\n\n### Tags\n\nIn the game's `<head>`:\n\n```html\n<meta name=\"hub:session\" content=\"1\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-players\" content=\"MIN-MAX\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-mode\" content=\"MODE\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-goal\" content=\"GOAL\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-howto\" content=\"CONTROLS\">\n```\n\n- `hub:session-players`: the smallest and largest number of players the game\n  takes in a session. The hub deals the game only when the number of players\n  is in that range.\n- `hub:session-mode`: `parallel`, `ghost` or `shared-world`.\n- `hub:session-goal` and `hub:session-howto`: how to win and the game's\n  controls, shown on the hub's card.\n\nOptional:\n\n- `hub:session-minutes`: how many minutes a round of the game takes. The hub\n  shows it and uses it to decide when to call time.\n- `hub:webgpu` with `required`: the game cannot run without WebGPU. The hub\n  then deals it only when every player's browser has WebGPU.\n\n### The client\n\n[session.js](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/session.js)\nis pasted into the game unmodified, as the first script in `<head>`, right\nafter `<meta charset>`. In a session it:\n\n- seeds `Math.random`, in parallel and ghost, before any of the game's own\n  scripts run, so it gives the same numbers on every copy;\n- gives the game an empty `localStorage` and `sessionStorage` of its own, so\n  nothing stored on the device carries into the round, and nothing the round\n  stores reaches the device's own storage;\n- hands `requestFullscreen()` and `exitFullscreen()` to the hub, which takes\n  its whole page fullscreen; `document.fullscreenElement` and\n  `fullscreenchange` follow the hub's page.\n\nThe hub replaces an unmodified copy of the client with each new version. An\nedited copy is not replaced.\n\n### Joining\n\n- `AIHub.active` is `true` from the first line when the hub opened the page.\n- In a session, the game opens straight into the round: no title screen,\n  menus or prompts before it, other than its own card (*The card*).\n- `AIHub.connect({ mode, seats: [min, max] })` returns a promise of the\n  round's `info`, or of `null` when there is no hub after all; with `null`\n  the game runs as it does on its own.\n- `AIHub.ready()` is called once, when the game has loaded and the round can\n  start, with no key press: the players answer the card.\n- The round starts when the card's countdown ends or every player pressed\n  Ready, and every game has called `ready()`. A game still loading then gets\n  20 more seconds; after that its player sits the round out.\n\n`info` (also on `AIHub` after `connect()`):\n\n| Field | |\n|---|---|\n| `me` | this copy's player id |\n| `players` | `[{ id, name, color }]`, ids `0..N-1` in seat order |\n| `host`, `isHost` | the id of the copy that runs a shared world, and whether it is this one |\n| `server` | `true` only on a copy that hosts a shared world with no player of its own |\n| `mode`, `round`, `limitMs` | the mode, the round number, and the round's hard limit after the start |\n| `seed` | a number, the same on every copy, behind `AIHub.rng(label)` |\n\nNames come from the hub and are never inserted into the page as HTML. Colours\nfollow the seat: `#e8443a`, `#3b82f6`, `#22c55e`, `#f5b700`.\n\n### The card\n\nBefore every round the players get 10 to 30 seconds to learn what comes\nnext and say when they are ready. By default the hub shows its own card over\nthe game. A game can make the card its own, as part of the game:\n\n```js\nAIHub.connect({ mode, seats, card: true });\n```\n\nThe hub's card then steps aside when the game calls `ready()`, and the game's\nscreen is the card until `start`. How it looks and sounds is the game's: its\ntitle, its music, its world, the players lining up. Introduce the game the way\nit deserves.\n\nWhile it is on, the card shows:\n\n- the game's name;\n- the players, each in their colour, and which of them are ready;\n- how to win the round;\n- the controls this player will use;\n- the time left, from the `card` event.\n\nAnd it takes two answers, from the keyboard, a controller, or a tap or click\non the card:\n\n- **Ready**: Enter, Cross (button 0), or a tap on Ready:\n  `AIHub.answer('ready')`.\n- **More time**: Triangle (button 3), a key the card names, or a tap on More\n  time: `AIHub.answer('more')`. Answering `more` again takes it back.\n\nNothing done on the card changes the round. It has no menus, settings or\nchoices, and play begins only at `start`. In parallel and ghost it draws no\nnumbers from `Math.random`, which would change the round's start: use\n`AIHub.rng('card')`.\n\n`card` arrives whenever it changes, and every second while the countdown runs:\n\n| Field | |\n|---|---|\n| `left` | milliseconds until the round starts by itself; `null` while paused or starting |\n| `paused` | `true` while most players asked for more time |\n| `starting` | `true` once the countdown is over or everyone is ready: `start` follows when every game has loaded |\n| `ready` | the ids of the players who are ready |\n| `asking` | how many players asked for more time (never who) |\n| `asked` | `true` when this player asked for more time |\n\n### The start\n\n`start` arrives when the round starts. Play begins three seconds later, when\n`AIHub.time()` reaches 0. `AIHub.time()` is the same timeline on every device,\ngive or take about 15 ms: negative during the countdown, `-Infinity` before\n`start`.\n\n### Reporting\n\n- `AIHub.progress({ score, label })`, in parallel and ghost: the player's\n  standing during the round. `score` is a number, higher is ahead; `label` is\n  text for the hub's scoreboard. The hub takes the latest about once a second.\n- `AIHub.result({ time })` or `AIHub.result({ score })`, in parallel and\n  ghost, once, when the player's round is over. `time` is milliseconds of\n  `AIHub.time()`, lower wins; `score` is a number, higher wins.\n- `AIHub.finish({ standings, scores, won })`, in a shared world, called once,\n  by the host only:\n  - `standings`: arrays of player ids, best first; players in the same array\n    tie. It lists every player still in the round once; anyone left out is\n    placed last.\n  - `scores` (optional): `{ id: number }`, shown on the scoreboard.\n  - `won` (optional): `true` or `false` when the round is a team result.\n\n### Time-up and the end\n\n- The hub may call time while the round is still going. On `time-up`, the\n  game reports within `graceMs`: a `result()` in parallel and ghost, a\n  `finish()` from the host in a shared world. A shared world with no\n  `finish()` by then is void.\n- `end` is the last message of a round. After it, the game takes no input and\n  sends nothing, and its sound stops. The hub shows its results over the\n  game, then removes it.\n\n| `end` reason | |\n|---|---|\n| `finished` | the round counted; `standings` is the final order |\n| `void` | it didn't count (no result, a fatal error, skipped) |\n| `host-left` | the host of a shared world left |\n| `sat-out` | this player missed the ready deadline |\n| `session-ended` | the session closed |\n\n### Leaving\n\n- `leave` arrives with `{ id, reason }` when a player leaves: `left`,\n  `disconnected`, `not-ready` or `kicked`. It is final for the round.\n- A parallel or ghost round goes on whoever leaves, the host included.\n- A shared-world round is void when its host leaves, isn't ready, or has its\n  tab hidden for more than 20 seconds.\n- `AIHub.fail(message)`: the game cannot run in this browser. From the host\n  of a shared world it voids the round; from any other copy it counts as\n  that player leaving.\n\n### Scoring\n\n- Parallel and ghost: players with a `time` rank first, lowest first; then\n  the rest by `score`. A player with no result is ranked by their last\n  progress.\n- Shared world: the host's `standings`. With `won`, the results show a team\n  result instead of medals.\n- Each player gets one point for every player they beat.\n\n`result()` and `finish()` may also carry `stats` and `awards`, shown with the\nresults:\n\n- in `result()`: `stats` is `{ name: value }` and `awards` is\n  `[{ title, detail }]`, for this player;\n- in `finish()`: `stats` is `{ id: { name: value } }` and `awards` is\n  `[{ id, title, detail }]`, for each player.\n\nPlaces and points come only from the standings, `time` and `score`.\n\n---\n\n## Sending data between copies\n\n### Parallel\n\nThe copies send nothing to each other. `send()` is not used.\n\n### Ghost\n\nEach copy sends its own player's position and what the player is doing to\nthe other copies with `send()`. Each copy shows the other players' characters\nonly while they are in the same area of the game as its own player, and those\ncharacters do not affect its world. `Math.random` is seeded as in parallel.\n\n### Shared world\n\n- The host's copy (`AIHub.isHost`) runs the world. The other copies send the\n  host what their own player does, and show the world the host sends them.\n- The hub can run the host's copy with no player of its own: `AIHub.server`\n  is `true` and `AIHub.me` is not among `AIHub.players`. The host's copy runs\n  the world in that case too, with no local player, camera or input.\n- `Math.random` is not seeded. `AIHub.rng(label)` gives the same numbers on\n  every copy.\n\n### `send()` and `message`\n\n- `AIHub.send(data, { to, reliable })` sends `data` to every other copy, or\n  to the one player `to`. It returns `false` when the message is dropped.\n- `AIHub.on('message', (data, from) => …)` receives it; `from` is the\n  sender's player id. A copy never receives its own messages. Messages sent\n  before another copy has loaded are queued for it.\n- `data` is JSON, at most 16 KB.\n- At most 20 messages a second leave each copy, with bursts up to 40; the\n  client drops the rest.\n- Reliable messages (the default) arrive in the order they were sent.\n  Messages sent with `reliable: false` may be lost or arrive out of order. An\n  unreliable message larger than about 1,200 bytes travels as several packets\n  and is lost whole if any of them is.\n\n---\n\n## Rules\n\nIn a session:\n\n- **Network only through the hub.** No WebSocket, WebRTC, or `fetch` to a\n  game server or public broker. Loading the game's own files is fine.\n- **No communication between players.** No chat, voice, emotes or custom\n  names. Names come from the hub.\n- **The page stays.** No `alert`, `confirm` or `prompt`; no `window.open`,\n  new tabs or navigating away. Quitting, restarting or returning to a title\n  screen does nothing; the hub starts and ends rounds.\n- **Create + Options is the hub's.** On a controller, holding the two\n  together opens the hub's corner bar; the game ignores Options while Create\n  is held.\n\nEverything on this page applies only in a session (`AIHub.active`). Outside\none, the game is not affected.\n\n---\n\n## Test it\n\nThe harness plays the hub: it loads the game 1–4 times on a simulated network\nand runs the checks the hub runs when a game joins the library. Serve it next\nto the game:\n\n```bash\ncurl -fsSO https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/harness.html\ncurl -fsSO https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/bridge.js\ncurl -fsSO https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/round.js\npython3 -m http.server 8000\n```\n\nThen open `http://localhost:8000/harness.html?game=GAME.html&players=2&auto=1`.\nThe hub's own test also runs ghost and shared-world games with\n`&players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1`, again with\n`&scenario=host-leave`, and shared worlds once more with\n`&players=2&scenario=server`.\n\nThe checklist fills in as it runs. **A game passes when\n`window.__hubCheck.pass` is true**; `document.body.dataset.complete` becomes\n`\"true\"` at the end. It checks:\n\n- the tags, `connect()`, `ready()` with no key press, and the start;\n- with the game's own card, that Enter answers Ready;\n- parallel and ghost: `Math.random` the same on every copy, and progress from\n  every copy; parallel sends nothing, ghost sends;\n- shared world: traffic both ways, and a round hosted by a copy with no\n  player of its own;\n- a player leaving, the host leaving, time-up, a valid result, and every copy\n  told the round ended;\n- no protocol problems, errors, dialogs, popups or sockets.\n\n**New round**, **Time up**, **Remove player** and **Hide host tab** run the\ncases by hand; clicking a player's frame gives it the keyboard and mouse.\n`&limit=` sets the round's length in seconds and `&seed=` fixes the seed. The\ngame is served from the harness's own origin.\n\nIn the AI Hub repository, `node scripts/hub-check.mjs <game>` runs the same\nchecks with Playwright, then opens the game outside a session to see it still\nruns there.\n\n---\n\n## Reference\n\n### Tags\n\n| Tag | |\n|---|---|\n| `hub:session` | `1`: this protocol |\n| `hub:session-players` | `MIN-MAX`: the number of players the game takes in a session |\n| `hub:session-mode` | `parallel`, `ghost` or `shared-world` |\n| `hub:session-goal` | how to win, shown on the hub's card |\n| `hub:session-howto` | the controls, shown on the hub's card |\n| `hub:session-minutes` | optional: how many minutes a round takes |\n| `hub:webgpu` | optional: `required` when the game cannot run without WebGPU |\n\n### API\n\n| | |\n|---|---|\n| `AIHub.active` | `true` in a session, from the first line |\n| `AIHub.connect({ mode, seats, card? })` | → `Promise<info \\| null>`; `null`: no hub. `card: true`: the game shows its own card |\n| `AIHub.ready()` | once, when the round can start |\n| `AIHub.answer('ready' \\| 'more')` | on the game's own card, before `start` |\n| `AIHub.time()` | milliseconds since play began: negative in the countdown, `-Infinity` before `start` |\n| `AIHub.on(event, fn)` | returns a function that removes the handler |\n| `AIHub.progress({ score, label })` | parallel and ghost |\n| `AIHub.result({ time \\| score, stats?, awards? })` | parallel and ghost, once |\n| `AIHub.finish({ standings, scores?, won?, stats?, awards? })` | shared world, the host, once |\n| `AIHub.send(data, { to, reliable })` | ghost and shared world |\n| `AIHub.rng(label)` | a generator of numbers in `[0, 1)`, the same on every copy, one stream per label |\n| `AIHub.seeded` | `true` when the client seeded `Math.random` |\n| `AIHub.fail(message)` | the game cannot run in this browser |\n\n`AIHub.probe()` and `AIHub.inspect()` exist for older games; the hub does not\nread them.\n\n| Event | Arguments |\n|---|---|\n| `card` | `{ left, paused, starting, ready, asking, asked }`, with the game's own card |\n| `start` | `{ in }`: milliseconds until play begins |\n| `message` | `data, from` |\n| `leave` | `{ id, reason }` |\n| `time-up` | `{ graceMs }` |\n| `end` | `{ reason, standings }` |\n\nEvents that arrive before a handler is attached are kept, and delivered in\norder when the first handler is attached. Fields and events a newer hub adds\nreach the game through the client unchanged.\n\n### Versions\n\nThis is protocol **1**, client **1.4.0**. Changes within version 1 only add:\ngames on older clients keep working. A change that would break a game becomes\nprotocol 2, with its own `hub:session` value.\n","numLines":411,"startLine":1,"totalLines":411}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01CyufMzj4H5Etn3bVeiCBpJ","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CghrdytWSqRoEL3JkMWoD","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_011uxBc796ZTjRWc4ZaxvCRv","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cat examples/arena.html | head -400","description":"Read the shared-world arena example"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7551,"cache_read_input_tokens":151414,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":7551},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9fe4bfc6-ee9b-4f5a-880a-60c3aeac1094","uuid":"3cf6015e-c5d9-4e6d-98a9-605609f1d7ff","timestamp":"2026-11-04T12:04:37.247Z","request_id":"req_011CghrdyXvZKdRDYGcDeGde","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_011uxBc796ZTjRWc4ZaxvCRv":{"command":"cat examples/arena.html | head -400","description":"Read the shared-world arena example"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011uxBc796ZTjRWc4ZaxvCRv","type":"tool_result","content":"<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n<meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\">\n<title>Star Arena — AI Hub session example (shared world)</title>\n<meta name=\"description\" content=\"A minimal shared-world game for the AI Hub Session Protocol: every copy moves its own player, the host runs the stars and the scores, first to ten wins.\">\n<meta name=\"theme-color\" content=\"#1b1530\">\n<meta name=\"hub:type\" content=\"Tech demo\">\n<meta name=\"hub:players\" content=\"1\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session\" content=\"1\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-players\" content=\"2-4\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-mode\" content=\"shared-world\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-minutes\" content=\"2\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-goal\" content=\"First to ten stars wins\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-howto\" content=\"Move: arrows, WASD or a stick · sprint: Space or Cross · or hold a finger\">\n<style>\n  html, body { margin: 0; height: 100%; background: #1b1530; color: #f3eef7; font: 16px system-ui, sans-serif; overflow: hidden; }\n  canvas { display: block; width: 100%; height: 100%; touch-action: none; }\n</style>\n<script>\n/*! aihub-session 1.4.0 — AI Hub Session Protocol v1 client. Paste it into your game unmodified. */\n(function (root) {\n  'use strict';\n  if (root.AIHub) return;\n\n  var VERSION = '1.4.0';\n  var HELLO_EVERY_MS = 500;\n  var HELLO_TIMEOUT_MS = 10000;\n  var PROGRESS_EVERY_MS = 1000;\n  /** The hub's welcome may change these; a newer hub never needs a newer copy of this file for it. */\n  var limits = { maxBytes: 16384, ratePerS: 20, burst: 40 };\n\n  var framed = false;\n  try {\n    framed = root.parent && root.parent !== root;\n  } catch (e) {\n    framed = true;\n  }\n  var search = String(root.location && root.location.search);\n  var flagged = /[?&]aihub=/.test(search);\n  var seedArg = /[?&]aihub-seed=(\\d+)/.exec(search);\n\n  var hub = {\n    version: VERSION,\n    protocol: 1,\n    /** True when the hub launched this page for a session (?aihub=1 inside a frame). */\n    active: !!(flagged && framed),\n    me: null,\n    host: null,\n    isHost: false,\n    players: [],\n    mode: null,\n    seed: 0,\n    limitMs: 0,\n    round: 0,\n    /** True when the hub shows the round's splash and collects every player's ready: call ready() once loaded, with no prompt. */\n    splash: false,\n    /** True when the hub seeded Math.random for this round (side by side): every copy draws the same numbers. */\n    seeded: false,\n  };\n\n  /** A storage that lives and dies with the page: the Storage methods, and items as properties too. */\n  function memoryStorage() {\n    var data = Object.create(null);\n    var api = {\n      getItem: function (k) {\n        k = String(k);\n        return k in data ? data[k] : null;\n      },\n      setItem: function (k, v) {\n        data[String(k)] = String(v);\n      },\n      removeItem: function (k) {\n        delete data[String(k)];\n      },\n      clear: function () {\n        for (var k in data) delete data[k];\n      },\n      key: function (i) {\n        var keys = Object.keys(data);\n        return i >= 0 && i < keys.length ? keys[i] : null;\n      },\n    };\n    if (typeof Proxy !== 'function') return api;\n    return new Proxy(api, {\n      get: function (t, k) {\n        if (k === 'length') return Object.keys(data).length;\n        if (typeof k === 'symbol' || k in t) return t[k];\n        return k in data ? data[k] : undefined;\n      },\n      set: function (t, k, v) {\n        if (typeof k !== 'symbol') data[k] = String(v);\n        return true;\n      },\n      has: function (t, k) {\n        return k in data || k in t;\n      },\n      deleteProperty: function (t, k) {\n        delete data[k];\n        return true;\n      },\n      ownKeys: function () {\n        return Object.keys(data);\n      },\n      getOwnPropertyDescriptor: function (t, k) {\n        return k in data ? { value: data[k], writable: true, enumerable: true, configurable: true } : undefined;\n      },\n    });\n  }\n\n  /** mulberry32: numbers in [0, 1), the same sequence everywhere for the same 32-bit start. */\n  function generator(a) {\n    return function () {\n      a = (a + 0x6d2b79f5) >>> 0;\n      var t = a;\n      t = Math.imul(t ^ (t >>> 15), t | 1);\n      t ^= t + Math.imul(t ^ (t >>> 7), t | 61);\n      return ((t ^ (t >>> 14)) >>> 0) / 4294967296;\n    };\n  }\n\n  // A fair start: in a session the game gets an empty storage of its own, so\n  // every round starts as a first launch (no saved unlocks, upgrades or runs),\n  // and nothing the round saves touches the player's own saves.\n  if (hub.active) {\n    for (var s = 0, stores = ['localStorage', 'sessionStorage']; s < stores.length; s++) {\n      try {\n        Object.defineProperty(root, stores[s], { configurable: true, value: memoryStorage() });\n      } catch (e) {\n        warn('could not give the game a fresh ' + stores[s]);\n      }\n    }\n  }\n\n  // Side by side: before any of the game's own scripts run, Math.random becomes\n  // a generator seeded by the hub, so every copy builds the same start.\n  var realRandom = Math.random;\n  var seededRandom = null;\n  if (hub.active && seedArg) {\n    Math.random = seededRandom = generator(Number(seedArg[1]) >>> 0);\n    hub.seeded = true;\n  }\n\n  // In a session the hub owns fullscreen: a game that asks for it gets the\n  // hub's whole page, so the scoreboard and the hub's cards stay on top. The\n  // hub says when its page goes in and out, so the game's own toggle and its\n  // fullscreenchange listeners work as they always did.\n  var fullscreenOn = false;\n  if (hub.active && root.Element && root.document) {\n    var asks = function (on) {\n      return function () {\n        post('fullscreen', { on: on });\n        return Promise.resolve();\n      };\n    };\n    var proto = root.Element.prototype;\n    proto.requestFullscreen = proto.webkitRequestFullscreen = asks(true);\n    root.document.exitFullscreen = root.document.webkitExitFullscreen = asks(false);\n    var shown = function () {\n      return fullscreenOn ? root.document.documentElement || null : null;\n    };\n    try {\n      Object.defineProperty(root.document, 'fullscreenElement', { configurable: true, get: shown });\n      Object.defineProperty(root.document, 'webkitFullscreenElement', { configurable: true, get: shown });\n    } catch (e) {}\n  }\n\n  /**\n   * No hub after all: play on, with Math.random the page's own again. The\n   * empty storage stays: the game has read it already, and what it writes\n   * must never land on the player's real saves.\n   */\n  function standAlone() {\n    hub.active = false;\n    if (seededRandom && Math.random === seededRandom) Math.random = realRandom;\n    hub.seeded = false;\n  }\n\n  var origin = '*';\n  var welcomed = false;\n  var ended = false;\n  var connecting = null;\n  var goAt = null;\n  var sentReady = false;\n  var reported = false;\n  var handlers = {};\n  var pending = {};\n  var tokens = limits.burst;\n  var refilled = now();\n  var probeFn = null;\n  var lastProgress = -Infinity;\n  var nextProgress = null;\n  var progressTimer = null;\n\n  function now() {\n    return root.performance && root.performance.now ? root.performance.now() : Date.now();\n  }\n\n  function warn(text) {\n    if (root.console) root.console.warn('[AIHub] ' + text);\n  }\n\n  function own(o, k) {\n    return Object.prototype.hasOwnProperty.call(o, k);\n  }\n\n  /** This client's own fields, which no welcome may overwrite. */\n  var KEEP = { aihub: 1, type: 1, version: 1, protocol: 1, active: 1, seeded: 1 };\n\n  /** A plain JSON copy, or undefined when it is not JSON. */\n  function json(value) {\n    try {\n      var text = JSON.stringify(value);\n      return text === undefined ? undefined : JSON.parse(text);\n    } catch (e) {\n      return undefined;\n    }\n  }\n\n  function post(type, fields) {\n    var msg = { aihub: 1, type: type };\n    for (var key in fields) if (own(fields, key)) msg[key] = fields[key];\n    try {\n      root.parent.postMessage(msg, origin);\n    } catch (e) {\n      warn('could not reach the hub: ' + e.message);\n    }\n  }\n\n  function emit(type, args) {\n    var list = handlers[type];\n    if (!list || !list.length || pending[type]) {\n      (pending[type] = pending[type] || []).push(args);\n      return;\n    }\n    for (var i = 0; i < list.length; i++) {\n      try {\n        list[i].apply(null, args);\n      } catch (e) {\n        setTimeout(function () {\n          throw e;\n        });\n      }\n    }\n  }\n\n  function onMessage(event) {\n    if (event.source !== root.parent) return;\n    var m = event.data;\n    if (!m || m.aihub !== 1 || typeof m.type !== 'string') return;\n    if (m.type === 'welcome') {\n      if (welcomed) return;\n      welcomed = true;\n      origin = event.origin && event.origin !== 'null' ? event.origin : '*';\n      // Every field the hub sends is kept, so a newer hub can add one without a newer client.\n      for (var key in m) {\n        if (!own(m, key) || KEEP[key] || typeof hub[key] === 'function') continue;\n        hub[key] = m[key];\n      }\n      hub.players = (m.players || []).slice();\n      hub.seed = m.seed >>> 0;\n      hub.isHost = m.me === m.host;\n      hub.splash = m.splash === true;\n      if (m.limits) {\n        for (var l in limits) if (own(limits, l) && Number(m.limits[l]) > 0) limits[l] = Number(m.limits[l]);\n        tokens = limits.burst;\n      }\n      if (connecting) connecting.resolve(info());\n      return;\n    }\n    if (m.type === 'fullscreen') {\n      fullscreenOn = m.on === true;\n      try {\n        root.document.dispatchEvent(new root.Event('fullscreenchange'));\n      } catch (e) {}\n      return;\n    }\n    if (!welcomed || ended) return;\n    if (m.type === 'start') {\n      goAt = now() + Number(m.in || 0);\n      emit('start', [{ in: Number(m.in || 0) }]);\n    } else if (m.type === 'message') {\n      emit('message', [m.data, m.from]);\n    } else if (m.type === 'leave') {\n      hub.players = hub.players.filter(function (p) {\n        return p.id !== m.id;\n      });\n      emit('leave', [{ id: m.id, reason: m.reason }]);\n    } else if (m.type === 'time-up') {\n      emit('time-up', [{ graceMs: m.graceMs }]);\n    } else if (m.type === 'end') {\n      ended = true;\n      if (progressTimer) clearTimeout(progressTimer);\n      emit('end', [{ reason: m.reason, standings: m.standings || null }]);\n    } else {\n      // An event this client has never heard of: hand it on as it came.\n      var detail = {};\n      for (var k in m) if (own(m, k) && k !== 'aihub' && k !== 'type') detail[k] = m[k];\n      emit(m.type, [detail]);\n    }\n  }\n\n  function info() {\n    var out = {};\n    for (var key in hub) if (own(hub, key) && typeof hub[key] !== 'function' && !KEEP[key]) out[key] = hub[key];\n    out.players = hub.players.slice();\n    return out;\n  }\n\n  /** Join the session. Resolves with the round's info, or null when there is no hub: play normally. */\n  hub.connect = function (opts) {\n    if (connecting) return connecting.promise;\n    var done;\n    var promise = new Promise(function (resolve) {\n      done = resolve;\n    });\n    connecting = { promise: promise, resolve: done };\n    if (!hub.active) {\n      done(null);\n      return promise;\n    }\n    opts = opts || {};\n    root.addEventListener('message', onMessage);\n    var started = now();\n    var hello = function () {\n      if (welcomed) return;\n      if (now() - started > HELLO_TIMEOUT_MS) {\n        standAlone();\n        warn('no hub answered; playing normally');\n        done(null);\n        return;\n      }\n      post('hello', { v: 1, client: VERSION, mode: opts.mode || null, seats: opts.seats || null, card: opts.card === true });\n      setTimeout(hello, HELLO_EVERY_MS);\n    };\n    hello();\n    return promise;\n  };\n\n  /** Everything is loaded: at once when info.splash, otherwise from the player's ready gesture. */\n  hub.ready = function () {\n    if (!welcomed || sentReady || ended) return;\n    sentReady = true;\n    post('ready', {});\n  };\n\n  /** On the game's own card (connect({ card: true })): this player is 'ready', or asks for 'more' time (again takes it back). */\n  hub.answer = function (what) {\n    if (!welcomed || ended || goAt !== null) return;\n    if (what !== 'ready' && what !== 'more') return warn('answer is ready or more');\n    post('answer', { answer: what });\n  };\n\n  hub.on = function (type, fn) {\n    (handlers[type] = handlers[type] || []).push(fn);\n    if (pending[type] && !pending[type].flushing) {\n      pending[type].flushing = true;\n      setTimeout(function () {\n        var queued = pending[type];\n        delete pending[type];\n        for (var i = 0; i < queued.length; i++) emit(type, queued[i]);\n      });\n    }\n    return function () {\n      var list = handlers[type] || [];\n      var at = list.indexOf(fn);\n      if (at !== -1) list.splice(at, 1);\n    };\n  };\n\n  /** Send JSON data to every other player, or to one with {to: id}. {reliable: false} may drop or reorder. */\n  hub.send = function (data, opts) {\n    if (!welcomed || ended) return false;\n    opts = opts || {};\n    var text;\n    try {\n      text = JSON.stringify(data);\n    } catch (e) {\n      warn('send: data is not JSON');\n      return false;\n    }\n    if (text === undefined) return false;\n    if (text.length > limits.maxBytes) {\n      warn('send: message over ' + limits.maxBytes + ' bytes dropped');\n      return false;\n    }\n    var t = now();\n    tokens = Math.min(limits.burst, tokens + ((t - refilled) / 1000) * limits.ratePerS);\n    refilled = t;\n    if (tokens < 1) {\n      warn('send: over ' + limits.ratePerS + ' messages a second, dropped');\n      return false;\n    }\n    tokens -= 1;\n    var fields = { data: JSON.parse(text), reliable: opts.reliable !== false };\n    if (opts.to !== undefined && opts.to !== null) fields.to = opts.to;\n    post('send', fields);\n    return true;\n  };","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9fe4bfc6-ee9b-4f5a-880a-60c3aeac1094","uuid":"59afd2b0-b9bc-4f6b-8921-a7f457445987","timestamp":"2026-11-04T12:04:37.259Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n<meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\">\n<title>Star Arena — AI Hub session example (shared world)</title>\n<meta name=\"description\" content=\"A minimal shared-world game for the AI Hub Session Protocol: every copy moves its own player, the host runs the stars and the scores, first to ten wins.\">\n<meta name=\"theme-color\" content=\"#1b1530\">\n<meta name=\"hub:type\" content=\"Tech demo\">\n<meta name=\"hub:players\" content=\"1\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session\" content=\"1\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-players\" content=\"2-4\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-mode\" content=\"shared-world\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-minutes\" content=\"2\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-goal\" content=\"First to ten stars wins\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-howto\" content=\"Move: arrows, WASD or a stick · sprint: Space or Cross · or hold a finger\">\n<style>\n  html, body { margin: 0; height: 100%; background: #1b1530; color: #f3eef7; font: 16px system-ui, sans-serif; overflow: hidden; }\n  canvas { display: block; width: 100%; height: 100%; touch-action: none; }\n</style>\n<script>\n/*! aihub-session 1.4.0 — AI Hub Session Protocol v1 client. Paste it into your game unmodified. */\n(function (root) {\n  'use strict';\n  if (root.AIHub) return;\n\n  var VERSION = '1.4.0';\n  var HELLO_EVERY_MS = 500;\n  var HELLO_TIMEOUT_MS = 10000;\n  var PROGRESS_EVERY_MS = 1000;\n  /** The hub's welcome may change these; a newer hub never needs a newer copy of this file for it. */\n  var limits = { maxBytes: 16384, ratePerS: 20, burst: 40 };\n\n  var framed = false;\n  try {\n    framed = root.parent && root.parent !== root;\n  } catch (e) {\n    framed = true;\n  }\n  var search = String(root.location && root.location.search);\n  var flagged = /[?&]aihub=/.test(search);\n  var seedArg = /[?&]aihub-seed=(\\d+)/.exec(search);\n\n  var hub = {\n    version: VERSION,\n    protocol: 1,\n    /** True when the hub launched this page for a session (?aihub=1 inside a frame). */\n    active: !!(flagged && framed),\n    me: null,\n    host: null,\n    isHost: false,\n    players: [],\n    mode: null,\n    seed: 0,\n    limitMs: 0,\n    round: 0,\n    /** True when the hub shows the round's splash and collects every player's ready: call ready() once loaded, with no prompt. */\n    splash: false,\n    /** True when the hub seeded Math.random for this round (side by side): every copy draws the same numbers. */\n    seeded: false,\n  };\n\n  /** A storage that lives and dies with the page: the Storage methods, and items as properties too. */\n  function memoryStorage() {\n    var data = Object.create(null);\n    var api = {\n      getItem: function (k) {\n        k = String(k);\n        return k in data ? data[k] : null;\n      },\n      setItem: function (k, v) {\n        data[String(k)] = String(v);\n      },\n      removeItem: function (k) {\n        delete data[String(k)];\n      },\n      clear: function () {\n        for (var k in data) delete data[k];\n      },\n      key: function (i) {\n        var keys = Object.keys(data);\n        return i >= 0 && i < keys.length ? keys[i] : null;\n      },\n    };\n    if (typeof Proxy !== 'function') return api;\n    return new Proxy(api, {\n      get: function (t, k) {\n        if (k === 'length') return Object.keys(data).length;\n        if (typeof k === 'symbol' || k in t) return t[k];\n        return k in data ? data[k] : undefined;\n      },\n      set: function (t, k, v) {\n        if (typeof k !== 'symbol') data[k] = String(v);\n        return true;\n      },\n      has: function (t, k) {\n        return k in data || k in t;\n      },\n      deleteProperty: function (t, k) {\n        delete data[k];\n        return true;\n      },\n      ownKeys: function () {\n        return Object.keys(data);\n      },\n      getOwnPropertyDescriptor: function (t, k) {\n        return k in data ? { value: data[k], writable: true, enumerable: true, configurable: true } : undefined;\n      },\n    });\n  }\n\n  /** mulberry32: numbers in [0, 1), the same sequence everywhere for the same 32-bit start. */\n  function generator(a) {\n    return function () {\n      a = (a + 0x6d2b79f5) >>> 0;\n      var t = a;\n      t = Math.imul(t ^ (t >>> 15), t | 1);\n      t ^= t + Math.imul(t ^ (t >>> 7), t | 61);\n      return ((t ^ (t >>> 14)) >>> 0) / 4294967296;\n    };\n  }\n\n  // A fair start: in a session the game gets an empty storage of its own, so\n  // every round starts as a first launch (no saved unlocks, upgrades or runs),\n  // and nothing the round saves touches the player's own saves.\n  if (hub.active) {\n    for (var s = 0, stores = ['localStorage', 'sessionStorage']; s < stores.length; s++) {\n      try {\n        Object.defineProperty(root, stores[s], { configurable: true, value: memoryStorage() });\n      } catch (e) {\n        warn('could not give the game a fresh ' + stores[s]);\n      }\n    }\n  }\n\n  // Side by side: before any of the game's own scripts run, Math.random becomes\n  // a generator seeded by the hub, so every copy builds the same start.\n  var realRandom = Math.random;\n  var seededRandom = null;\n  if (hub.active && seedArg) {\n    Math.random = seededRandom = generator(Number(seedArg[1]) >>> 0);\n    hub.seeded = true;\n  }\n\n  // In a session the hub owns fullscreen: a game that asks for it gets the\n  // hub's whole page, so the scoreboard and the hub's cards stay on top. The\n  // hub says when its page goes in and out, so the game's own toggle and its\n  // fullscreenchange listeners work as they always did.\n  var fullscreenOn = false;\n  if (hub.active && root.Element && root.document) {\n    var asks = function (on) {\n      return function () {\n        post('fullscreen', { on: on });\n        return Promise.resolve();\n      };\n    };\n    var proto = root.Element.prototype;\n    proto.requestFullscreen = proto.webkitRequestFullscreen = asks(true);\n    root.document.exitFullscreen = root.document.webkitExitFullscreen = asks(false);\n    var shown = function () {\n      return fullscreenOn ? root.document.documentElement || null : null;\n    };\n    try {\n      Object.defineProperty(root.document, 'fullscreenElement', { configurable: true, get: shown });\n      Object.defineProperty(root.document, 'webkitFullscreenElement', { configurable: true, get: shown });\n    } catch (e) {}\n  }\n\n  /**\n   * No hub after all: play on, with Math.random the page's own again. The\n   * empty storage stays: the game has read it already, and what it writes\n   * must never land on the player's real saves.\n   */\n  function standAlone() {\n    hub.active = false;\n    if (seededRandom && Math.random === seededRandom) Math.random = realRandom;\n    hub.seeded = false;\n  }\n\n  var origin = '*';\n  var welcomed = false;\n  var ended = false;\n  var connecting = null;\n  var goAt = null;\n  var sentReady = false;\n  var reported = false;\n  var handlers = {};\n  var pending = {};\n  var tokens = limits.burst;\n  var refilled = now();\n  var probeFn = null;\n  var lastProgress = -Infinity;\n  var nextProgress = null;\n  var progressTimer = null;\n\n  function now() {\n    return root.performance && root.performance.now ? root.performance.now() : Date.now();\n  }\n\n  function warn(text) {\n    if (root.console) root.console.warn('[AIHub] ' + text);\n  }\n\n  function own(o, k) {\n    return Object.prototype.hasOwnProperty.call(o, k);\n  }\n\n  /** This client's own fields, which no welcome may overwrite. */\n  var KEEP = { aihub: 1, type: 1, version: 1, protocol: 1, active: 1, seeded: 1 };\n\n  /** A plain JSON copy, or undefined when it is not JSON. */\n  function json(value) {\n    try {\n      var text = JSON.stringify(value);\n      return text === undefined ? undefined : JSON.parse(text);\n    } catch (e) {\n      return undefined;\n    }\n  }\n\n  function post(type, fields) {\n    var msg = { aihub: 1, type: type };\n    for (var key in fields) if (own(fields, key)) msg[key] = fields[key];\n    try {\n      root.parent.postMessage(msg, origin);\n    } catch (e) {\n      warn('could not reach the hub: ' + e.message);\n    }\n  }\n\n  function emit(type, args) {\n    var list = handlers[type];\n    if (!list || !list.length || pending[type]) {\n      (pending[type] = pending[type] || []).push(args);\n      return;\n    }\n    for (var i = 0; i < list.length; i++) {\n      try {\n        list[i].apply(null, args);\n      } catch (e) {\n        setTimeout(function () {\n          throw e;\n        });\n      }\n    }\n  }\n\n  function onMessage(event) {\n    if (event.source !== root.parent) return;\n    var m = event.data;\n    if (!m || m.aihub !== 1 || typeof m.type !== 'string') return;\n    if (m.type === 'welcome') {\n      if (welcomed) return;\n      welcomed = true;\n      origin = event.origin && event.origin !== 'null' ? event.origin : '*';\n      // Every field the hub sends is kept, so a newer hub can add one without a newer client.\n      for (var key in m) {\n        if (!own(m, key) || KEEP[key] || typeof hub[key] === 'function') continue;\n        hub[key] = m[key];\n      }\n      hub.players = (m.players || []).slice();\n      hub.seed = m.seed >>> 0;\n      hub.isHost = m.me === m.host;\n      hub.splash = m.splash === true;\n      if (m.limits) {\n        for (var l in limits) if (own(limits, l) && Number(m.limits[l]) > 0) limits[l] = Number(m.limits[l]);\n        tokens = limits.burst;\n      }\n      if (connecting) connecting.resolve(info());\n      return;\n    }\n    if (m.type === 'fullscreen') {\n      fullscreenOn = m.on === true;\n      try {\n        root.document.dispatchEvent(new root.Event('fullscreenchange'));\n      } catch (e) {}\n      return;\n    }\n    if (!welcomed || ended) return;\n    if (m.type === 'start') {\n      goAt = now() + Number(m.in || 0);\n      emit('start', [{ in: Number(m.in || 0) }]);\n    } else if (m.type === 'message') {\n      emit('message', [m.data, m.from]);\n    } else if (m.type === 'leave') {\n      hub.players = hub.players.filter(function (p) {\n        return p.id !== m.id;\n      });\n      emit('leave', [{ id: m.id, reason: m.reason }]);\n    } else if (m.type === 'time-up') {\n      emit('time-up', [{ graceMs: m.graceMs }]);\n    } else if (m.type === 'end') {\n      ended = true;\n      if (progressTimer) clearTimeout(progressTimer);\n      emit('end', [{ reason: m.reason, standings: m.standings || null }]);\n    } else {\n      // An event this client has never heard of: hand it on as it came.\n      var detail = {};\n      for (var k in m) if (own(m, k) && k !== 'aihub' && k !== 'type') detail[k] = m[k];\n      emit(m.type, [detail]);\n    }\n  }\n\n  function info() {\n    var out = {};\n    for (var key in hub) if (own(hub, key) && typeof hub[key] !== 'function' && !KEEP[key]) out[key] = hub[key];\n    out.players = hub.players.slice();\n    return out;\n  }\n\n  /** Join the session. Resolves with the round's info, or null when there is no hub: play normally. */\n  hub.connect = function (opts) {\n    if (connecting) return connecting.promise;\n    var done;\n    var promise = new Promise(function (resolve) {\n      done = resolve;\n    });\n    connecting = { promise: promise, resolve: done };\n    if (!hub.active) {\n      done(null);\n      return promise;\n    }\n    opts = opts || {};\n    root.addEventListener('message', onMessage);\n    var started = now();\n    var hello = function () {\n      if (welcomed) return;\n      if (now() - started > HELLO_TIMEOUT_MS) {\n        standAlone();\n        warn('no hub answered; playing normally');\n        done(null);\n        return;\n      }\n      post('hello', { v: 1, client: VERSION, mode: opts.mode || null, seats: opts.seats || null, card: opts.card === true });\n      setTimeout(hello, HELLO_EVERY_MS);\n    };\n    hello();\n    return promise;\n  };\n\n  /** Everything is loaded: at once when info.splash, otherwise from the player's ready gesture. */\n  hub.ready = function () {\n    if (!welcomed || sentReady || ended) return;\n    sentReady = true;\n    post('ready', {});\n  };\n\n  /** On the game's own card (connect({ card: true })): this player is 'ready', or asks for 'more' time (again takes it back). */\n  hub.answer = function (what) {\n    if (!welcomed || ended || goAt !== null) return;\n    if (what !== 'ready' && what !== 'more') return warn('answer is ready or more');\n    post('answer', { answer: what });\n  };\n\n  hub.on = function (type, fn) {\n    (handlers[type] = handlers[type] || []).push(fn);\n    if (pending[type] && !pending[type].flushing) {\n      pending[type].flushing = true;\n      setTimeout(function () {\n        var queued = pending[type];\n        delete pending[type];\n        for (var i = 0; i < queued.length; i++) emit(type, queued[i]);\n      });\n    }\n    return function () {\n      var list = handlers[type] || [];\n      var at = list.indexOf(fn);\n      if (at !== -1) list.splice(at, 1);\n    };\n  };\n\n  /** Send JSON data to every other player, or to one with {to: id}. {reliable: false} may drop or reorder. */\n  hub.send = function (data, opts) {\n    if (!welcomed || ended) return false;\n    opts = opts || {};\n    var text;\n    try {\n      text = JSON.stringify(data);\n    } catch (e) {\n      warn('send: data is not JSON');\n      return false;\n    }\n    if (text === undefined) return false;\n    if (text.length > limits.maxBytes) {\n      warn('send: message over ' + limits.maxBytes + ' bytes dropped');\n      return false;\n    }\n    var t = now();\n    tokens = Math.min(limits.burst, tokens + ((t - refilled) / 1000) * limits.ratePerS);\n    refilled = t;\n    if (tokens < 1) {\n      warn('send: over ' + limits.ratePerS + ' messages a second, dropped');\n      return false;\n    }\n    tokens -= 1;\n    var fields = { data: JSON.parse(text), reliable: opts.reliable !== false };\n    if (opts.to !== undefined && opts.to !== null) fields.to = opts.to;\n    post('send', fields);\n    return true;\n  };","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_011uxBc796ZTjRWc4ZaxvCRv","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CghreAUVRgqp9cnWDCGZJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01YEUTSjhN8tGDeWHvJfzhxB","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"sed -n '/<\\/script>/,$p' examples/arena.html | sed -n '1,400p' | head -330","description":"Read the arena example's game script"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5522,"cache_read_input_tokens":158965,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5522},"output_tokens":20,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9fe4bfc6-ee9b-4f5a-880a-60c3aeac1094","uuid":"8633bdec-a829-4512-bb22-eea342892d07","timestamp":"2026-11-04T12:04:39.911Z","request_id":"req_011CghreA8fRwNc2SsEk72ct","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01YEUTSjhN8tGDeWHvJfzhxB":{"command":"sed -n '/<\\/script>/,$p' examples/arena.html | sed -n '1,400p' | head -330","description":"Read the arena example's game script"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01YEUTSjhN8tGDeWHvJfzhxB","type":"tool_result","content":"</script>\n</head>\n<body>\n<canvas id=\"c\" aria-label=\"Star Arena\"></canvas>\n<script>\n'use strict';\n// Star Arena: the smallest honest shared-world game, the plain form of \"Shared\n// world\" (lib/hub/README.md): the host runs the world. Every copy moves its own\n// player from its own stick, at once, and never waits for the network to do\n// it. The host's copy runs only what is shared, the star and the scores:\n//   me     each other copy → the host, ~15 a second, unreliable: where my player is\n//   s      the host → everyone, ~15 a second, unreliable: every player, its score, the star\n//   claim  a copy → the host, reliable, once a star: my player touched star n\n//   pick   the host → everyone, reliable: player id took star n\n// The host takes each player where it says it is, and a claim scores unless\n// someone else got there first. A last snapshot, reliable, ends the round.\n// The host may be a server, a copy with no player of its own (AIHub.server):\n// it runs the same host code, moves nobody and draws nothing.\n// First to TARGET stars wins.\nconst W = 800, H = 600, R = 18, SPEED = 260, TARGET = 10;\nconst canvas = document.getElementById('c');\nconst ctx = canvas.getContext('2d');\nconst keys = new Set();\nlet pointer = null;\nlet audio = null;\n\naddEventListener('keydown', (e) => {\n  if (e.key === 'Escape') return toggleMenu();\n  if (menu.open) return menuKey(e.key);\n  keys.add(e.key.toLowerCase());\n  gesture();\n});\naddEventListener('keyup', (e) => keys.delete(e.key.toLowerCase()));\ncanvas.addEventListener('pointerdown', (e) => { pointer = e; gesture(); });\ncanvas.addEventListener('pointermove', (e) => { if (pointer) pointer = e; });\naddEventListener('pointerup', () => { pointer = null; });\n\nfunction beep(freq) {\n  if (!audio || muted) return;\n  const o = audio.createOscillator(), g = audio.createGain();\n  o.frequency.value = freq; g.gain.value = 0.05;\n  o.connect(g).connect(audio.destination);\n  o.start(); o.stop(audio.currentTime + 0.08);\n}\n\n// ---- the controller, in the browser's standard mapping (a PS5 DualSense:\n// Cross 0, Circle 1, Triangle 3, Create 8, Options 9, D-pad 12-15, left stick\n// axes 0 and 1). Buttons count on the frame they go down.\nconst PAD = { cross: 0, circle: 1, triangle: 3, create: 8, options: 9, up: 12, down: 13 };\nlet pad = null, padNow = [], padWas = [];\nfunction readPad() {\n  pad = navigator.getGamepads ? [...navigator.getGamepads()].find((p) => p && p.connected) || null : null;\n  padWas = padNow;\n  padNow = pad ? pad.buttons.map((b) => b.pressed) : [];\n  // Create + Options is the hub's: it opens the hub's corner bar, so Options alone opens the menu.\n  if (pressed(PAD.options) && !padNow[PAD.create]) return toggleMenu();\n  if (menu.open) {\n    if (pressed(PAD.up)) menuKey('ArrowUp');\n    if (pressed(PAD.down)) menuKey('ArrowDown');\n    if (pressed(PAD.cross)) menuKey('Enter');\n    if (pressed(PAD.circle)) toggleMenu();\n  } else if (padNow.some((b, i) => b && !padWas[i] && i !== PAD.create && i !== PAD.options)) gesture();\n}\nconst pressed = (b) => !!padNow[b] && !padWas[b];\n\n// ---- the settings menu: Esc or Options, over the running game. It never\n// pauses anything; while it is open your player simply stands still.\nlet muted = false;\nconst menu = {\n  open: false,\n  at: 0,\n  items: [\n    { label: () => `Sound: ${muted ? 'off' : 'on'}`, act: () => { muted = !muted; } },\n    { label: () => 'Back to the game', act: () => toggleMenu() },\n  ],\n};\nfunction toggleMenu() { menu.open = !menu.open; menu.at = 0; keys.clear(); }\nfunction menuKey(key) {\n  if (key === 'ArrowUp' || key === 'w') menu.at = (menu.at + menu.items.length - 1) % menu.items.length;\n  if (key === 'ArrowDown' || key === 's') menu.at = (menu.at + 1) % menu.items.length;\n  if (key === 'Enter' || key === ' ') menu.items[menu.at].act();\n}\n\n/** The local stick: keys, the first gamepad, or a held pointer. Still while the menu is open. */\nfunction stick(me) {\n  if (menu.open) return { x: 0, y: 0, sprint: false };\n  let x = 0, y = 0;\n  if (keys.has('arrowleft') || keys.has('a')) x -= 1;\n  if (keys.has('arrowright') || keys.has('d')) x += 1;\n  if (keys.has('arrowup') || keys.has('w')) y -= 1;\n  if (keys.has('arrowdown') || keys.has('s')) y += 1;\n  if (pad) {\n    if (Math.abs(pad.axes[0]) > 0.2) x = pad.axes[0];\n    if (Math.abs(pad.axes[1]) > 0.2) y = pad.axes[1];\n    if (padNow[12]) y = -1;\n    if (padNow[13]) y = 1;\n    if (padNow[14]) x = -1;\n    if (padNow[15]) x = 1;\n  }\n  if (pointer && me) {\n    const p = toWorld(pointer);\n    const dx = p.x - me.x, dy = p.y - me.y, d = Math.hypot(dx, dy);\n    if (d > 8) { x = dx / d; y = dy / d; }\n  }\n  const sprint = keys.has(' ') || !!padNow[PAD.cross] || !!padNow[7];\n  const len = Math.hypot(x, y);\n  return len > 1 ? { x: x / len, y: y / len, sprint } : { x, y, sprint };\n}\n\nfunction toWorld(e) {\n  const r = canvas.getBoundingClientRect(), s = Math.min(r.width / W, r.height / H);\n  return { x: (e.clientX - r.left - (r.width - W * s) / 2) / s, y: (e.clientY - r.top - (r.height - H * s) / 2) / s };\n}\n\n// ---- state shared by both modes\nconst game = {\n  phase: 'title',            // title | waiting | playing | over\n  players: [],               // {id, name, color, x, y, score, gone}, drawn at x, y\n  star: { x: W / 2, y: H / 2, n: 0 },   // n numbers the stars, so a claim names the one it touched\n  rng: Math.random,\n  message: '',\n  standings: null,\n};\nlet felt = { x: 0, y: 0, sprint: false };   // the local stick as last read\n\nfunction place(players) {\n  players.forEach((p, i) => {\n    const a = (i / Math.max(players.length, 1)) * Math.PI * 2;\n    p.tx = p.x = W / 2 + Math.cos(a) * 200; p.ty = p.y = H / 2 + Math.sin(a) * 180;\n  });\n}\nfunction newStar() {\n  game.star = { x: 40 + game.rng() * (W - 80), y: 40 + game.rng() * (H - 80), n: game.star.n + 1 };\n}\n\n/** Your own player, from your own stick. Every copy moves its own, every frame, host or not. */\nfunction move(p, s, dt) {\n  const speed = SPEED * (s.sprint ? 1.5 : 1);\n  p.x = Math.max(R, Math.min(W - R, p.x + s.x * speed * dt));\n  p.y = Math.max(R, Math.min(H - R, p.y + s.y * speed * dt));\n}\nconst touching = (p) => Math.hypot(p.x - game.star.x, p.y - game.star.y) < R + 12;\n\n// ---- solo: the game as it plays on its own\nfunction solo() {\n  game.players = [{ id: 0, name: 'You', color: '#f5b700', x: W / 2, y: H / 2, score: 0 }];\n  game.phase = 'title';\n  game.message = 'Star Arena — press any key or tap to play';\n}\nlet soloEnds = 0;\n\n// ---- hub mode. Every other player also has tx, ty: where it last said it is\n// (and on the host, at: when). It is drawn easing toward there; your own player\n// is drawn where you put it.\nlet hub = null;\nlet lastSent = 0;\nlet lastSnap = -Infinity;    // the newest snapshot taken, by its AIHub.time()\nlet claimed = -1;            // the star this copy claimed last: one claim a star\n\nasync function connect() {\n  const info = await AIHub.connect({ mode: 'shared-world', seats: [2, 4] });\n  if (!info) return solo();\n  hub = info;\n  game.rng = AIHub.rng('stars');\n  game.players = info.players.map((p) => ({ ...p, x: 0, y: 0, score: 0, gone: false, at: -Infinity }));\n  place(game.players);\n  newStar();                 // the first star comes from the seed: the same on every copy\n  // The hub's card collects everyone's ready: ready up as soon as the arena is built.\n  game.phase = 'waiting';\n  game.message = 'Get ready…';\n  AIHub.ready();\n  AIHub.on('start', () => { game.phase = 'playing'; unlockAudio(); });\n  AIHub.on('message', (data, from) => {\n    if (hub.isHost && data.t === 'me') heard(from, data);\n    if (hub.isHost && data.t === 'claim') take(from, data.n);\n    if (from === hub.host && data.t === 's') applySnapshot(data);\n    if (from === hub.host && data.t === 'pick' && data.id !== hub.me) beep(330);   // your own cheered at the claim\n  });\n  AIHub.on('leave', ({ id }) => {\n    const p = game.players.find((q) => q.id === id);\n    if (p) p.gone = true;\n    if (hub.isHost && game.phase === 'playing' && game.players.filter((q) => !q.gone).length < 2) finish();\n  });\n  AIHub.on('time-up', () => { if (hub.isHost) finish(); });\n  AIHub.on('end', ({ reason, standings }) => {\n    game.phase = 'over';\n    game.standings = standings;\n    game.message = reason === 'finished' ? 'Round over' : reason === 'sat-out' ? 'You sat this one out' : 'Round cancelled';\n  });\n}\nconst inside = (v, max) => Math.max(R, Math.min(max - R, Number(v) || 0));\n\n/** Host: a player says where it is, and there it is, unless an older report arrived late. */\nfunction heard(id, m) {\n  const p = game.players.find((q) => q.id === id);\n  if (!p || !(m.at > p.at)) return;\n  p.at = m.at; p.tx = inside(m.x, W); p.ty = inside(m.y, H);\n}\n\n/** Host: player id touched star n. It scores, unless someone else got there first. */\nfunction take(id, n) {\n  const p = game.players.find((q) => q.id === id);\n  if (game.phase !== 'playing' || !p || p.gone || n !== game.star.n) return;\n  p.score++;\n  newStar();\n  beep(id === hub.me ? 660 : 330);\n  AIHub.send({ t: 'pick', id, n });\n  if (p.score >= TARGET) finish();\n}\n\n/** Host: one snapshot for everyone: every player still here with its score, and the star. */\nfunction snapshot() {\n  const spot = (p) => (p.id === hub.me ? [p.x, p.y] : [p.tx, p.ty]);   // the others: where they said\n  return {\n    t: 's',\n    at: Math.round(AIHub.time()),\n    p: game.players.filter((p) => !p.gone).map((p) => [p.id, ...spot(p).map(Math.round), p.score]),\n    s: [Math.round(game.star.x), Math.round(game.star.y), game.star.n],\n  };\n}\n\n/** Not the host: take the scores, the star and the other players from the snapshot, never your own player. */\nfunction applySnapshot(s) {\n  if (s.at < lastSnap) return;   // unreliable: an older one that arrived late\n  lastSnap = s.at;\n  for (const [id, x, y, score] of s.p) {\n    const p = game.players.find((q) => q.id === id);\n    if (!p) continue;\n    p.score = score;\n    if (id !== hub.me) { p.tx = x; p.ty = y; }\n  }\n  game.star = { x: s.s[0], y: s.s[1], n: s.s[2] };\n  if (s.over) { game.phase = 'over'; game.message = 'Round over'; }\n}\n\n/** Host: standings by score, ties together, best first. A last snapshot, reliable, ends every copy on the same scores. */\nfunction finish() {\n  if (game.phase === 'over') return;\n  AIHub.send({ ...snapshot(), over: 1 });\n  const live = game.players.filter((p) => !p.gone).sort((a, b) => b.score - a.score);\n  const standings = [];\n  for (const p of live) {\n    const last = standings[standings.length - 1];\n    if (last && last.score === p.score) last.ids.push(p.id);\n    else standings.push({ score: p.score, ids: [p.id] });\n  }\n  const scores = Object.fromEntries(game.players.map((p) => [p.id, p.score]));\n  AIHub.finish({ standings: standings.map((g) => g.ids), scores });\n  game.phase = 'over';\n  game.message = 'Round over';\n}\n\nfunction unlockAudio() {\n  if (!audio) {\n    try { audio = new AudioContext(); } catch { audio = null; }\n  }\n  audio?.resume?.().catch(() => {});\n}\n\nfunction gesture() {\n  unlockAudio();\n  if (!hub && (game.phase === 'title' || game.phase === 'over')) {\n    solo();\n    game.phase = 'playing';\n    soloEnds = performance.now() + 60_000;\n  }\n}\n\n// ---- the loop: advance by elapsed time, never pause\nlet last = performance.now();\nfunction frame(now) {\n  const dt = Math.min((now - last) / 1000, 0.25);\n  last = now;\n  readPad();\n  const me = game.players.find((p) => p.id === (hub ? hub.me : 0));\n  felt = stick(me);\n  if (game.phase === 'playing' && (!hub || AIHub.time() >= 0)) {\n    if (me) move(me, felt, dt);   // now, on every copy: your controls never wait for the network\n    if (hub) play(now, dt, me);\n    else {\n      if (touching(me)) { me.score++; newStar(); beep(660); }\n      if (now > soloEnds) { game.phase = 'over'; game.message = `Time! ${me.score} stars — press to play again`; }\n    }\n  }\n  if (!hub?.server) draw(now);   // a server runs the world and needs no picture of it\n  requestAnimationFrame(frame);\n}\n\n/** A session frame, after your own move: the star, what this copy sends, and the others eased toward where they are. */\nfunction play(now, dt, me) {\n  if (me && touching(me)) {\n    if (hub.isHost) take(hub.me, game.star.n);\n    else if (claimed !== game.star.n) {\n      // Predict the contact: claim the star once, hide it and cheer now. The host decides the point.\n      claimed = game.star.n;\n      AIHub.send({ t: 'claim', n: claimed }, { to: hub.host });\n      beep(660);\n    }\n  }\n  if (game.phase === 'playing' && now - lastSent > 66) {\n    lastSent = now;\n    if (hub.isHost) AIHub.send(snapshot(), { reliable: false });\n    else AIHub.send({ t: 'me', at: Math.round(AIHub.time()), x: Math.round(me.x), y: Math.round(me.y) }, { to: hub.host, reliable: false });\n  }\n  const k = 1 - Math.pow(0.001, dt);\n  for (const p of game.players) if (p !== me) { p.x += (p.tx - p.x) * k; p.y += (p.ty - p.y) * k; }\n}\n\nfunction draw(now) {\n  const r = canvas.getBoundingClientRect();\n  const dpr = devicePixelRatio || 1;\n  if (canvas.width !== Math.round(r.width * dpr) || canvas.height !== Math.round(r.height * dpr)) {\n    canvas.width = Math.round(r.width * dpr); canvas.height = Math.round(r.height * dpr);\n  }\n  const s = Math.min(canvas.width / W, canvas.height / H);\n  ctx.setTransform(1, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0);\n  ctx.fillStyle = '#120e22'; ctx.fillRect(0, 0, canvas.width, canvas.height);\n  ctx.setTransform(s, 0, 0, s, (canvas.width - W * s) / 2, (canvas.height - H * s) / 2);\n  ctx.fillStyle = '#1b1530'; ctx.fillRect(0, 0, W, H);\n\n  if (game.star.n !== claimed) {   // a star you claimed is gone here until the host's next one arrives\n    ctx.fillStyle = '#ffd34d';\n    ctx.beginPath(); ctx.arc(game.star.x, game.star.y, 10 + Math.sin(now / 150) * 2, 0, Math.PI * 2); ctx.fill();\n  }\n\n  ctx.textAlign = 'center';\n  for (const p of game.players) {\n    if (p.gone) continue;\n    ctx.fillStyle = p.color;\n    ctx.beginPath(); ctx.arc(p.x, p.y, R, 0, Math.PI * 2); ctx.fill();","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9fe4bfc6-ee9b-4f5a-880a-60c3aeac1094","uuid":"92e14baa-2404-44ce-a766-a2262bdbdee2","timestamp":"2026-11-04T12:04:39.929Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"</script>\n</head>\n<body>\n<canvas id=\"c\" aria-label=\"Star Arena\"></canvas>\n<script>\n'use strict';\n// Star Arena: the smallest honest shared-world game, the plain form of \"Shared\n// world\" (lib/hub/README.md): the host runs the world. Every copy moves its own\n// player from its own stick, at once, and never waits for the network to do\n// it. The host's copy runs only what is shared, the star and the scores:\n//   me     each other copy → the host, ~15 a second, unreliable: where my player is\n//   s      the host → everyone, ~15 a second, unreliable: every player, its score, the star\n//   claim  a copy → the host, reliable, once a star: my player touched star n\n//   pick   the host → everyone, reliable: player id took star n\n// The host takes each player where it says it is, and a claim scores unless\n// someone else got there first. A last snapshot, reliable, ends the round.\n// The host may be a server, a copy with no player of its own (AIHub.server):\n// it runs the same host code, moves nobody and draws nothing.\n// First to TARGET stars wins.\nconst W = 800, H = 600, R = 18, SPEED = 260, TARGET = 10;\nconst canvas = document.getElementById('c');\nconst ctx = canvas.getContext('2d');\nconst keys = new Set();\nlet pointer = null;\nlet audio = null;\n\naddEventListener('keydown', (e) => {\n  if (e.key === 'Escape') return toggleMenu();\n  if (menu.open) return menuKey(e.key);\n  keys.add(e.key.toLowerCase());\n  gesture();\n});\naddEventListener('keyup', (e) => keys.delete(e.key.toLowerCase()));\ncanvas.addEventListener('pointerdown', (e) => { pointer = e; gesture(); });\ncanvas.addEventListener('pointermove', (e) => { if (pointer) pointer = e; });\naddEventListener('pointerup', () => { pointer = null; });\n\nfunction beep(freq) {\n  if (!audio || muted) return;\n  const o = audio.createOscillator(), g = audio.createGain();\n  o.frequency.value = freq; g.gain.value = 0.05;\n  o.connect(g).connect(audio.destination);\n  o.start(); o.stop(audio.currentTime + 0.08);\n}\n\n// ---- the controller, in the browser's standard mapping (a PS5 DualSense:\n// Cross 0, Circle 1, Triangle 3, Create 8, Options 9, D-pad 12-15, left stick\n// axes 0 and 1). Buttons count on the frame they go down.\nconst PAD = { cross: 0, circle: 1, triangle: 3, create: 8, options: 9, up: 12, down: 13 };\nlet pad = null, padNow = [], padWas = [];\nfunction readPad() {\n  pad = navigator.getGamepads ? [...navigator.getGamepads()].find((p) => p && p.connected) || null : null;\n  padWas = padNow;\n  padNow = pad ? pad.buttons.map((b) => b.pressed) : [];\n  // Create + Options is the hub's: it opens the hub's corner bar, so Options alone opens the menu.\n  if (pressed(PAD.options) && !padNow[PAD.create]) return toggleMenu();\n  if (menu.open) {\n    if (pressed(PAD.up)) menuKey('ArrowUp');\n    if (pressed(PAD.down)) menuKey('ArrowDown');\n    if (pressed(PAD.cross)) menuKey('Enter');\n    if (pressed(PAD.circle)) toggleMenu();\n  } else if (padNow.some((b, i) => b && !padWas[i] && i !== PAD.create && i !== PAD.options)) gesture();\n}\nconst pressed = (b) => !!padNow[b] && !padWas[b];\n\n// ---- the settings menu: Esc or Options, over the running game. It never\n// pauses anything; while it is open your player simply stands still.\nlet muted = false;\nconst menu = {\n  open: false,\n  at: 0,\n  items: [\n    { label: () => `Sound: ${muted ? 'off' : 'on'}`, act: () => { muted = !muted; } },\n    { label: () => 'Back to the game', act: () => toggleMenu() },\n  ],\n};\nfunction toggleMenu() { menu.open = !menu.open; menu.at = 0; keys.clear(); }\nfunction menuKey(key) {\n  if (key === 'ArrowUp' || key === 'w') menu.at = (menu.at + menu.items.length - 1) % menu.items.length;\n  if (key === 'ArrowDown' || key === 's') menu.at = (menu.at + 1) % menu.items.length;\n  if (key === 'Enter' || key === ' ') menu.items[menu.at].act();\n}\n\n/** The local stick: keys, the first gamepad, or a held pointer. Still while the menu is open. */\nfunction stick(me) {\n  if (menu.open) return { x: 0, y: 0, sprint: false };\n  let x = 0, y = 0;\n  if (keys.has('arrowleft') || keys.has('a')) x -= 1;\n  if (keys.has('arrowright') || keys.has('d')) x += 1;\n  if (keys.has('arrowup') || keys.has('w')) y -= 1;\n  if (keys.has('arrowdown') || keys.has('s')) y += 1;\n  if (pad) {\n    if (Math.abs(pad.axes[0]) > 0.2) x = pad.axes[0];\n    if (Math.abs(pad.axes[1]) > 0.2) y = pad.axes[1];\n    if (padNow[12]) y = -1;\n    if (padNow[13]) y = 1;\n    if (padNow[14]) x = -1;\n    if (padNow[15]) x = 1;\n  }\n  if (pointer && me) {\n    const p = toWorld(pointer);\n    const dx = p.x - me.x, dy = p.y - me.y, d = Math.hypot(dx, dy);\n    if (d > 8) { x = dx / d; y = dy / d; }\n  }\n  const sprint = keys.has(' ') || !!padNow[PAD.cross] || !!padNow[7];\n  const len = Math.hypot(x, y);\n  return len > 1 ? { x: x / len, y: y / len, sprint } : { x, y, sprint };\n}\n\nfunction toWorld(e) {\n  const r = canvas.getBoundingClientRect(), s = Math.min(r.width / W, r.height / H);\n  return { x: (e.clientX - r.left - (r.width - W * s) / 2) / s, y: (e.clientY - r.top - (r.height - H * s) / 2) / s };\n}\n\n// ---- state shared by both modes\nconst game = {\n  phase: 'title',            // title | waiting | playing | over\n  players: [],               // {id, name, color, x, y, score, gone}, drawn at x, y\n  star: { x: W / 2, y: H / 2, n: 0 },   // n numbers the stars, so a claim names the one it touched\n  rng: Math.random,\n  message: '',\n  standings: null,\n};\nlet felt = { x: 0, y: 0, sprint: false };   // the local stick as last read\n\nfunction place(players) {\n  players.forEach((p, i) => {\n    const a = (i / Math.max(players.length, 1)) * Math.PI * 2;\n    p.tx = p.x = W / 2 + Math.cos(a) * 200; p.ty = p.y = H / 2 + Math.sin(a) * 180;\n  });\n}\nfunction newStar() {\n  game.star = { x: 40 + game.rng() * (W - 80), y: 40 + game.rng() * (H - 80), n: game.star.n + 1 };\n}\n\n/** Your own player, from your own stick. Every copy moves its own, every frame, host or not. */\nfunction move(p, s, dt) {\n  const speed = SPEED * (s.sprint ? 1.5 : 1);\n  p.x = Math.max(R, Math.min(W - R, p.x + s.x * speed * dt));\n  p.y = Math.max(R, Math.min(H - R, p.y + s.y * speed * dt));\n}\nconst touching = (p) => Math.hypot(p.x - game.star.x, p.y - game.star.y) < R + 12;\n\n// ---- solo: the game as it plays on its own\nfunction solo() {\n  game.players = [{ id: 0, name: 'You', color: '#f5b700', x: W / 2, y: H / 2, score: 0 }];\n  game.phase = 'title';\n  game.message = 'Star Arena — press any key or tap to play';\n}\nlet soloEnds = 0;\n\n// ---- hub mode. Every other player also has tx, ty: where it last said it is\n// (and on the host, at: when). It is drawn easing toward there; your own player\n// is drawn where you put it.\nlet hub = null;\nlet lastSent = 0;\nlet lastSnap = -Infinity;    // the newest snapshot taken, by its AIHub.time()\nlet claimed = -1;            // the star this copy claimed last: one claim a star\n\nasync function connect() {\n  const info = await AIHub.connect({ mode: 'shared-world', seats: [2, 4] });\n  if (!info) return solo();\n  hub = info;\n  game.rng = AIHub.rng('stars');\n  game.players = info.players.map((p) => ({ ...p, x: 0, y: 0, score: 0, gone: false, at: -Infinity }));\n  place(game.players);\n  newStar();                 // the first star comes from the seed: the same on every copy\n  // The hub's card collects everyone's ready: ready up as soon as the arena is built.\n  game.phase = 'waiting';\n  game.message = 'Get ready…';\n  AIHub.ready();\n  AIHub.on('start', () => { game.phase = 'playing'; unlockAudio(); });\n  AIHub.on('message', (data, from) => {\n    if (hub.isHost && data.t === 'me') heard(from, data);\n    if (hub.isHost && data.t === 'claim') take(from, data.n);\n    if (from === hub.host && data.t === 's') applySnapshot(data);\n    if (from === hub.host && data.t === 'pick' && data.id !== hub.me) beep(330);   // your own cheered at the claim\n  });\n  AIHub.on('leave', ({ id }) => {\n    const p = game.players.find((q) => q.id === id);\n    if (p) p.gone = true;\n    if (hub.isHost && game.phase === 'playing' && game.players.filter((q) => !q.gone).length < 2) finish();\n  });\n  AIHub.on('time-up', () => { if (hub.isHost) finish(); });\n  AIHub.on('end', ({ reason, standings }) => {\n    game.phase = 'over';\n    game.standings = standings;\n    game.message = reason === 'finished' ? 'Round over' : reason === 'sat-out' ? 'You sat this one out' : 'Round cancelled';\n  });\n}\nconst inside = (v, max) => Math.max(R, Math.min(max - R, Number(v) || 0));\n\n/** Host: a player says where it is, and there it is, unless an older report arrived late. */\nfunction heard(id, m) {\n  const p = game.players.find((q) => q.id === id);\n  if (!p || !(m.at > p.at)) return;\n  p.at = m.at; p.tx = inside(m.x, W); p.ty = inside(m.y, H);\n}\n\n/** Host: player id touched star n. It scores, unless someone else got there first. */\nfunction take(id, n) {\n  const p = game.players.find((q) => q.id === id);\n  if (game.phase !== 'playing' || !p || p.gone || n !== game.star.n) return;\n  p.score++;\n  newStar();\n  beep(id === hub.me ? 660 : 330);\n  AIHub.send({ t: 'pick', id, n });\n  if (p.score >= TARGET) finish();\n}\n\n/** Host: one snapshot for everyone: every player still here with its score, and the star. */\nfunction snapshot() {\n  const spot = (p) => (p.id === hub.me ? [p.x, p.y] : [p.tx, p.ty]);   // the others: where they said\n  return {\n    t: 's',\n    at: Math.round(AIHub.time()),\n    p: game.players.filter((p) => !p.gone).map((p) => [p.id, ...spot(p).map(Math.round), p.score]),\n    s: [Math.round(game.star.x), Math.round(game.star.y), game.star.n],\n  };\n}\n\n/** Not the host: take the scores, the star and the other players from the snapshot, never your own player. */\nfunction applySnapshot(s) {\n  if (s.at < lastSnap) return;   // unreliable: an older one that arrived late\n  lastSnap = s.at;\n  for (const [id, x, y, score] of s.p) {\n    const p = game.players.find((q) => q.id === id);\n    if (!p) continue;\n    p.score = score;\n    if (id !== hub.me) { p.tx = x; p.ty = y; }\n  }\n  game.star = { x: s.s[0], y: s.s[1], n: s.s[2] };\n  if (s.over) { game.phase = 'over'; game.message = 'Round over'; }\n}\n\n/** Host: standings by score, ties together, best first. A last snapshot, reliable, ends every copy on the same scores. */\nfunction finish() {\n  if (game.phase === 'over') return;\n  AIHub.send({ ...snapshot(), over: 1 });\n  const live = game.players.filter((p) => !p.gone).sort((a, b) => b.score - a.score);\n  const standings = [];\n  for (const p of live) {\n    const last = standings[standings.length - 1];\n    if (last && last.score === p.score) last.ids.push(p.id);\n    else standings.push({ score: p.score, ids: [p.id] });\n  }\n  const scores = Object.fromEntries(game.players.map((p) => [p.id, p.score]));\n  AIHub.finish({ standings: standings.map((g) => g.ids), scores });\n  game.phase = 'over';\n  game.message = 'Round over';\n}\n\nfunction unlockAudio() {\n  if (!audio) {\n    try { audio = new AudioContext(); } catch { audio = null; }\n  }\n  audio?.resume?.().catch(() => {});\n}\n\nfunction gesture() {\n  unlockAudio();\n  if (!hub && (game.phase === 'title' || game.phase === 'over')) {\n    solo();\n    game.phase = 'playing';\n    soloEnds = performance.now() + 60_000;\n  }\n}\n\n// ---- the loop: advance by elapsed time, never pause\nlet last = performance.now();\nfunction frame(now) {\n  const dt = Math.min((now - last) / 1000, 0.25);\n  last = now;\n  readPad();\n  const me = game.players.find((p) => p.id === (hub ? hub.me : 0));\n  felt = stick(me);\n  if (game.phase === 'playing' && (!hub || AIHub.time() >= 0)) {\n    if (me) move(me, felt, dt);   // now, on every copy: your controls never wait for the network\n    if (hub) play(now, dt, me);\n    else {\n      if (touching(me)) { me.score++; newStar(); beep(660); }\n      if (now > soloEnds) { game.phase = 'over'; game.message = `Time! ${me.score} stars — press to play again`; }\n    }\n  }\n  if (!hub?.server) draw(now);   // a server runs the world and needs no picture of it\n  requestAnimationFrame(frame);\n}\n\n/** A session frame, after your own move: the star, what this copy sends, and the others eased toward where they are. */\nfunction play(now, dt, me) {\n  if (me && touching(me)) {\n    if (hub.isHost) take(hub.me, game.star.n);\n    else if (claimed !== game.star.n) {\n      // Predict the contact: claim the star once, hide it and cheer now. The host decides the point.\n      claimed = game.star.n;\n      AIHub.send({ t: 'claim', n: claimed }, { to: hub.host });\n      beep(660);\n    }\n  }\n  if (game.phase === 'playing' && now - lastSent > 66) {\n    lastSent = now;\n    if (hub.isHost) AIHub.send(snapshot(), { reliable: false });\n    else AIHub.send({ t: 'me', at: Math.round(AIHub.time()), x: Math.round(me.x), y: Math.round(me.y) }, { to: hub.host, reliable: false });\n  }\n  const k = 1 - Math.pow(0.001, dt);\n  for (const p of game.players) if (p !== me) { p.x += (p.tx - p.x) * k; p.y += (p.ty - p.y) * k; }\n}\n\nfunction draw(now) {\n  const r = canvas.getBoundingClientRect();\n  const dpr = devicePixelRatio || 1;\n  if (canvas.width !== Math.round(r.width * dpr) || canvas.height !== Math.round(r.height * dpr)) {\n    canvas.width = Math.round(r.width * dpr); canvas.height = Math.round(r.height * dpr);\n  }\n  const s = Math.min(canvas.width / W, canvas.height / H);\n  ctx.setTransform(1, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0);\n  ctx.fillStyle = '#120e22'; ctx.fillRect(0, 0, canvas.width, canvas.height);\n  ctx.setTransform(s, 0, 0, s, (canvas.width - W * s) / 2, (canvas.height - H * s) / 2);\n  ctx.fillStyle = '#1b1530'; ctx.fillRect(0, 0, W, H);\n\n  if (game.star.n !== claimed) {   // a star you claimed is gone here until the host's next one arrives\n    ctx.fillStyle = '#ffd34d';\n    ctx.beginPath(); ctx.arc(game.star.x, game.star.y, 10 + Math.sin(now / 150) * 2, 0, Math.PI * 2); ctx.fill();\n  }\n\n  ctx.textAlign = 'center';\n  for (const p of game.players) {\n    if (p.gone) continue;\n    ctx.fillStyle = p.color;\n    ctx.beginPath(); ctx.arc(p.x, p.y, R, 0, Math.PI * 2); ctx.fill();","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01YEUTSjhN8tGDeWHvJfzhxB","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
