{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01M6KLrGN35ycAgKfo9BqWF4","type":"tool_result","content":"18:  (play the game's own bot, start(1, { demo: true }): DEMO shows, no table), 'scores' for o.scores seconds (6) once\n47:  constructor(game, o = {}) {\n63:  start(players = 1, o = {}) {\n72:  add(points, at) {\n82:  die() {\n94:  coin() { if (this.credits === null) return null; this.credits++; this.game.audio.sfx('coin'); return this.credits; }\n97:  continue(seconds = 10, done) { this._cont = { t: seconds, done }; this.game.input.consumeAll(); }\n101:  table(mode = '') { const k = 'arcade:' + this.id + ':' + mode, t = KEPT[k] || E.store.get(k, null); return Array.isArray(t) ? t.slice() : []; }\n103:  qualifies(score, mode = '') { const t = this.table(mode); return !this.demo && score > 0 && (t.length < 10 || score > t[t.length - 1].score); }\n105:  enter(score, mode = '', done) { this.entry = { score, mode, name: [0, 0, 0], i: 0, done, t: 0 }; this.game.input.consumeAll(); }\n107:  card(text, seconds = 2) { this._cards.push({ text, t: seconds, big: true }); }\n109:  say(text, seconds = 1.2) { this._cards.push({ text, t: seconds, big: false }); }\n111:  clear() { this._cards.length = 0; }\n116:  attract(dt) {\n125:  wake() { this.phase = 'title'; this._idle = 0; }\n127:  endDemo() { this.phase = 'scores'; this._idle = 0; }\n129:  update(dt) {\n170:  draw(r, box) {\n204:  drawTable(r, mode = '', y = 40, title = 'HIGH SCORES') {\n14:  cab.enter(score, mode, done): initials on a letter wheel (up and down turn it, left and right move, confirm takes a\n15-  letter; taps on its arrows and OK do each); cab.entry is it while open. cab.drawTable(r, mode, y, title).\n16-- cab.card('STAGE 2', 2) shows a card (cab.carding while one is up), cab.say('READY!') a word under it.\n17-- The attract mode, on the title: cab.attract(dt) -> 'title', then 'demo' once o.idle seconds (20) pass without input\n18-  (play the game's own bot, start(1, { demo: true }): DEMO shows, no table), 'scores' for o.scores seconds (6) once\n19-  cab.endDemo() is called or o.demo seconds (30) pass, then 'title'; any input goes back to 'title'.\n20-- cab.update(dt) every step (cards, the entry, the continue); cab.draw(r, [x, y, w, h]) after your drawing: the HUD\n21-  (in the playfield's box: the screen when none), cards, DEMO, the continue and the entry.\n22-\n23-```js arcade\n24-const E = My3D2dge, game = new E.Game({ headless: true }), cab = new E.Arcade(game, { id: 'doc', lives: 2, extra: [500] });\n25-cab.start(1); cab.add(300); cab.add(300);\n26-if (cab.p.score !== 600 || cab.p.lives !== 3) throw new Error('extra life');\n27-if (cab.die() !== 'again' || cab.die() !== 'again' || cab.die() !== 'over') throw new Error('lives');\n28-cab.start(2); if (cab.die() !== 'next' || cab.p.n !== 2) throw new Error('turns');\n29-```\n30-Rules: tables live in E.store ('arcade:' + id + ':' + mode; kept for the visit where storage is blocked); a demo is the game's own bot (or a recorded input log)\n31-playing the real rules; the entry and the continue read the game's keys, so hold play while either is open.\n32-*/\n33-(function (E) {\n34-'use strict';\n35-if (!E) throw new Error('my-3D2dge module ARCADE: load engine/my-3d2dge.js (or the agent edition) first');\n36-\n--\n105:  enter(score, mode = '', done) { this.entry = { score, mode, name: [0, 0, 0], i: 0, done, t: 0 }; this.game.input.consumeAll(); }\n106-  /** a card in the middle of the screen for seconds ('STAGE 2', 'PLAYER 2, READY!') */\n107-  card(text, seconds = 2) { this._cards.push({ text, t: seconds, big: true }); }\n108-  /** a short word under the cards for seconds ('READY!', 'EXTRA LIFE!') */\n109-  say(text, seconds = 1.2) { this._cards.push({ text, t: seconds, big: false }); }\n110-  /** take every card and word down */\n111-  clear() { this._cards.length = 0; }\n112-  /** is a card up? (hold play while it is) */\n113-  get carding() { return this._cards.some(c => c.big); }\n114-  /*