{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019zZtYY9tRkvUz34vyJVUDi","type":"tool_result","content":"210:- `E.sprite(rows, colors = {}, scale = 1)`: Pixel sprite written as strings. Each character is one pixel; colors maps a character to a hex color; '.' and ' ' are transparent. scale (whole number) enlarges each pixel. const COIN = E.sprite(['.yy.', 'yYYy', 'yYYy', '.yy.'], { y: '#f0b020', Y: '#fff0a0' }); Draw it with r.sprite(x, y, z, COIN) (depth sorted) or px.sprite(g, COIN, sx, sy).\n215:- `E.anim(frames, fps = 8, o = {})` †: frames to play: anim([spr1, spr2, spr3], fps = 8, { loop: true, pingpong: false }), or anim(sheet, 8, { frames: 4 }) for several frames side by side in one sprite's rows. Draw it with r.sprite(x, y, z, a, { t }) (t: its clock, seconds; the game's time by default); a.frame(t) is the sprite at time t, a.index(t) its number, a.duration one play (seconds)\n418:- `r.decal(fn, o)`: draw on the floor before the queue. opts.emissive (0..1) makes it glow under GPU lighting\n420:- `r.groundArc(x, y, r0, r1, a0, a1, color, alpha = 1, z = 0, g = this.tgt)`: a band of a ring on the ground from radius r0 to r1 and angle a0 to a1 (radians): melee telegraphs, sight cones\n421:- `r.groundDisc(x, y, rad, color, alpha = 1, z = 0)`: a dithered disc lying on the ground (radius in world units, z its height): shadows, auras, area attacks\n423:- `r.groundRing(x, y, rad, color, alpha = 1, z = 0)`: a ring lying on the ground (radius in world units)\n433:- `r.sprite(x, y, z, spr, o = {})`: Queue a pixel sprite (from E.sprite) standing at world point (x, y, z). Depth sorted like an actor. opts: { flip, anchor: 'bottom' (feet on the point, default; E.shapeSprite's: its own feet) | 'center' | 'top', glow: 0..1, bias, flash, outline, alpha, xray, ghost (the last five use the actor path), t (an E.anim's clock: spr may be one), rot (radians, about its center: anchor 'center' unless given), steps (16), scale, wrap: [w, h] (a world that wraps round: a copy across each edge it crosses; w alone wraps x) }\n436:- `r.textAt(x, y, z, str, color = '#ffffff', o = {})`: text floating at a world point (names, prompts): r.textAt(x, y, z, 'OPEN', '#ffe08a')\n439:- `r.visible(x, y, z = 0, mx = 60, up = 30, down = 90)`: is a world point near the visible area? margins in pixels (characters extend upward from their feet)\n440:- `r.w(x, y, z = 0)`: world -> buffer pixel coords\n444:- `r.ix`, `r.iy`: the camera's whole-pixel offset this frame (a world point is at r.w(x, y, z) on the buffer)\n678:- `rig.worldOffset(p)`: where a point in the rig's own frame ([forward, right, up]; a joint such as rig.J.head, or one offset from it) sits, in world units from the rig's feet: add rig.x, y, z for the world point, or project it to draw at a joint\n680:- `rig.J`: its joints this step in its own frame ({ hipL, kneeL, footL, shC, head, handR, ... }; rig.worldOffset(J.handR) gives one in the world)\n703:- `E.MOVES: slash, backslash, overhead, rising, thrust, spin, plunge, twohand, jab, cross, hook, uppercut, haymaker, elbow, ... (24)`: a library of named attacks with timing and body motion (anticipation, lunge, step, twist, hop). new E.Attack('overhead'), new E.Attack('thrust', { reach: 10 }), new E.Combo(['jab', 'cross', 'hook', 'uppercut']) rig.update(dt, { ..., attack: E.move('roundhouse', .5) }) // any move at any moment, for previews and cutscenes The same move works on every build and in every view: heights are relative to the shoulders (rel: true), reaches scale with arm length, and horizontal swings turn into screen-plane swings in side views. A move's spec fields:\n709:- `E.move(name, u = .5, phase = 'active')`: any move from E.MOVES at any moment, for previews and cutscenes: rig.update(dt, { ..., attack: E.move('roundhouse', .5) }) (u 0..1 through phase)","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9fe4bfc6-ee9b-4f5a-880a-60c3aeac1094","uuid":"ca5034ba-d29b-4157-8ddc-d3ed470fd2df","timestamp":"2026-11-04T12:26:10.761Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"210:- `E.sprite(rows, colors = {}, scale = 1)`: Pixel sprite written as strings. Each character is one pixel; colors maps a character to a hex color; '.' and ' ' are transparent. scale (whole number) enlarges each pixel. const COIN = E.sprite(['.yy.', 'yYYy', 'yYYy', '.yy.'], { y: '#f0b020', Y: '#fff0a0' }); Draw it with r.sprite(x, y, z, COIN) (depth sorted) or px.sprite(g, COIN, sx, sy).\n215:- `E.anim(frames, fps = 8, o = {})` †: frames to play: anim([spr1, spr2, spr3], fps = 8, { loop: true, pingpong: false }), or anim(sheet, 8, { frames: 4 }) for several frames side by side in one sprite's rows. Draw it with r.sprite(x, y, z, a, { t }) (t: its clock, seconds; the game's time by default); a.frame(t) is the sprite at time t, a.index(t) its number, a.duration one play (seconds)\n418:- `r.decal(fn, o)`: draw on the floor before the queue. opts.emissive (0..1) makes it glow under GPU lighting\n420:- `r.groundArc(x, y, r0, r1, a0, a1, color, alpha = 1, z = 0, g = this.tgt)`: a band of a ring on the ground from radius r0 to r1 and angle a0 to a1 (radians): melee telegraphs, sight cones\n421:- `r.groundDisc(x, y, rad, color, alpha = 1, z = 0)`: a dithered disc lying on the ground (radius in world units, z its height): shadows, auras, area attacks\n423:- `r.groundRing(x, y, rad, color, alpha = 1, z = 0)`: a ring lying on the ground (radius in world units)\n433:- `r.sprite(x, y, z, spr, o = {})`: Queue a pixel sprite (from E.sprite) standing at world point (x, y, z). Depth sorted like an actor. opts: { flip, anchor: 'bottom' (feet on the point, default; E.shapeSprite's: its own feet) | 'center' | 'top', glow: 0..1, bias, flash, outline, alpha, xray, ghost (the last five use the actor path), t (an E.anim's clock: spr may be one), rot (radians, about its center: anchor 'center' unless given), steps (16), scale, wrap: [w, h] (a world that wraps round: a copy across each edge it crosses; w alone wraps x) }\n436:- `r.textAt(x, y, z, str, color = '#ffffff', o = {})`: text floating at a world point (names, prompts): r.textAt(x, y, z, 'OPEN', '#ffe08a')\n439:- `r.visible(x, y, z = 0, mx = 60, up = 30, down = 90)`: is a world point near the visible area? margins in pixels (characters extend upward from their feet)\n440:- `r.w(x, y, z = 0)`: world -> buffer pixel coords\n444:- `r.ix`, `r.iy`: the camera's whole-pixel offset this frame (a world point is at r.w(x, y, z) on the buffer)\n678:- `rig.worldOffset(p)`: where a point in the rig's own frame ([forward, right, up]; a joint such as rig.J.head, or one offset from it) sits, in world units from the rig's feet: add rig.x, y, z for the world point, or project it to draw at a joint\n680:- `rig.J`: its joints this step in its own frame ({ hipL, kneeL, footL, shC, head, handR, ... }; rig.worldOffset(J.handR) gives one in the world)\n703:- `E.MOVES: slash, backslash, overhead, rising, thrust, spin, plunge, twohand, jab, cross, hook, uppercut, haymaker, elbow, ... (24)`: a library of named attacks with timing and body motion (anticipation, lunge, step, twist, hop). new E.Attack('overhead'), new E.Attack('thrust', { reach: 10 }), new E.Combo(['jab', 'cross', 'hook', 'uppercut']) rig.update(dt, { ..., attack: E.move('roundhouse', .5) }) // any move at any moment, for previews and cutscenes The same move works on every build and in every view: heights are relative to the shoulders (rel: true), reaches scale with arm length, and horizontal swings turn into screen-plane swings in side views. A move's spec fields:\n709:- `E.move(name, u = .5, phase = 'active')`: any move from E.MOVES at any moment, for previews and cutscenes: rig.update(dt, { ..., attack: E.move('roundhouse', .5) }) (u 0..1 through phase)","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_019zZtYY9tRkvUz34vyJVUDi","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
